 1000000000A10A3AA9983245BDDD5BF9B0281994
SUMMARY:CVL Submission Team
DESCRIPTION:•       Status\n•       What do we do with changes to the metamo
 del or the language at this point in time?\no       We should not do too muc
 h in this period\, but of course fixing "bugs" should be possible.\no       
 I would like to agree on a straight strategy for this.\n•       Logo\no     
   CVL has not had any attractive logo. Now there is a suggestion inspired by
  the logos of similar languages.\n\n\n\n\n\nOystein Haugen invites you to an
  online meeting using WebEx.\n\nMeeting Number: 161 162 080\nMeeting Passwor
 d: abrakadabra\n\n-------------------------------------------------------\nT
 o join this meeting (Now from mobile devices!)\n----------------------------
 ---------------------------\n1. Go to https://sintef.webex.com/sintef/j.php?
 J=161162080&PW=NZDcxZmRhOWMx\n2. If requested\, enter your name and email ad
 dress.\n3. If a password is required\, enter the meeting password: abrakadab
 ra\n4. Click "Join".\n5. Follow the instructions that appear on your screen.
 \n\n\n\n-------------------------------------------------------\nAudio confe
 rence information\n-------------------------------------------------------\n
 To receive a call back\, provide your phone number when you join the meeting
 \, or call the number below and enter the access code.\nCall-in toll number 
 (UK): +44-20-310-64804\nGlobal call-in numbers: https://sintef.webex.com/sin
 tef/globalcallin.php?serviceType=MC&ED=1587497&tollFree=0\n\nAccess code:161
  162 080\n\nhttp://www.webex.com\n\n\n\nIMPORTANT NOTICE: This WebEx service
  includes a feature that allows audio and any documents and other materials 
 exchanged or viewed during the session to be recorded. By joining this sessi
 on\, you automatically consent to such recordings. If you do not consent to 
 the recording\, discuss your concerns with the meeting host prior to the sta
 rt of the recording or do not join the session. Please note that any such re
 cordings may be subject to discovery in the event of litigation.\n\n
LOCATION:WebEx
