 Quang \, Inria\n\nS1.2\n\n11:25 AM\n\n00:10:00\n\n\nMachine-Learning based h
 eader compression and authentication for IoT\n\nCyril Morin\, Inria\n\nS1.3\
 n\n\nSession 2: Network information theory and machine learning\n\n11:35 AM\
 n\n00:10:00\n\nSummary of common lab research on Network Information and Lea
 rning Optimization\n\nCédric Adjih\, Inria\n\nS2.1\n\n11:45 AM\n\n00:15:00\n
 \nNon Orthoganal Multiple Access  for IoT\n\nCédric Adjih\, Inria\n\nS2.2\n\
 n12:00 PM\n\n00:10:00\n\nSummary of common lab research on Distributed Learn
 ing and Control for Network Analysis\n\nGerard Burnside\, Nokia\nKonstantin 
 Avrachenkov\, Inria\n\nS2.3\n\n12:10 PM\n\n00:15:00\n\nTitle to be confirmed
 \n\nEitan Altman\, Inria\n\nS2.4\n\n12:25 PM\n\n00:10:00\n\nAsynchronous dis
 tributed semi-supervised learning\n\nMaximilien Dreveton\, Inria\n\nS2.5\n\n
 12:35 PM\n\n01:30:00\n\nlunch and networking\n\n2:05 PM\n\n00:40:00\n\nKeyno
 te: "Some Issues with Deep Learning"\n\nMarc Schoenauer\, Inria\n\nK2\n\n\nS
