SUMMARY:CVL Submission Team
DESCRIPTION:Main feature is Concrete Syntax.\nEverybody should find examples
  of concrete syntax.\nIn particular we will focus on\n1.      The graphical 
 notation for VSpecs\n2.      The principles behind textual syntax (Jean-Marc
 )\n3.      Examples of highlighting used for Variation Points\n\nFollowing u
 p last week’s discussion:\nQ&A on Configurable Units – please comment off-li
 ne on Ran’s presentation (on the SVN)\n\nPlease notice that there will be NO
  CVL WebEx on 18. April and 25. April due to Easter vacation. (Very long vac
 ation in Norway)\n\n\n\nOystein Haugen invites you to an online meeting usin
 g WebEx.\n\nMeeting Number: 846 820 805\nMeeting Password: abrakadabra\n\n--
 -----------------------------------------------------\nTo join this meeting 
 (Now from mobile devices!)\n------------------------------------------------
 -------\n1. Go to https://sintef.webex.com/sintef/j.php?J=846820805&PW=NMTQz
 MjhiODcy\n2. If requested\, enter your name and email address.\n3. If a pass
 word is required\, enter the meeting password: abrakadabra\n4. Click "Join".
 \n5. Follow the instructions that appear on your screen.\n\n\n\n------------
 -------------------------------------------\nAudio conference information\n-
 ------------------------------------------------------\nTo receive a call ba
 ck\, provide your phone number when you join the meeting\, or call the numbe
 r below and enter the access code.\nCall-in toll number (UK): (0)20 700 5100
 0\nGlobal call-in numbers: https://sintef.webex.com/sintef/globalcallin.php?
 serviceType=MC&ED=165318852&tollFree=0\n\nAccess code:846 820 805\n\nhttp://
 www.webex.com\n\n\n\nIMPORTANT NOTICE: This WebEx service includes a feature
  that allows audio and any documents and other materials exchanged or viewed
  during the session to be recorded. By joining this session\, you automatica
 lly consent to such recordings. If you do not consent to the recording\, dis
 cuss your concerns with the meeting host prior to the start of the recording
  or do not join the session. Please note that any such recordings may be sub
 ject to discovery in the event of litigation.\n\n
LOCATION:WebEx
