BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:0949e6e5-aba5-44bf-b48c-d00321fc7e47
SUMMARY:[SEMINAR] Context-aware Energy Demand Shifting for Domestic Energy M
 icro-generation (Jacky BOURGEOIS)
DESCRIPTION:Abstract: Distributed micro-generation is considered one of the 
 cornerstones of the future energy infrastructure and residential energy gene
 ration using solar panels\, heat pumps\, etc. has become a feasible option f
 or most homeowners. Yet practical savings fall far short of this target for 
 three reasons: (a) residential energy production and consumption are out of 
 sync\, (b) the practice of turning self-generated energy into money via feed
 -in tariffs essentially makes energy production invisible (c) and the availa
 ble of seemingly free energy (after investment) undermines attempts to use f
 eedback mechanisms to change people's energy behaviour in a positive way. Pa
 st research has focused on energy demand reduction\, looking at the technolo
 gical\, human and social issues. In contrast\, energy generation has not yet
  been a focus of investigation in computing and human computer interaction r
 esearch. My research will investigate energy demand shifting to help consume
 rs narrow the gap between the amount of energy they produce and the amount o
 f energy they generate by answering the research question: Is the combinatio
 n of accurate algorithms and useful HCIs an effective way to synchronize ene
 rgy micro-generation and energy consumption while maintaining user comfort a
 nd user acceptability in residential context?
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<html><body><h3>La réunion suivante a été modif
 iée :</h3>\n\n<p>\n<table border='0'>\n<tr><th align=left>Sujet :</th><td>[S
 EMINAR] Context-aware Energy Demand Shifting for Domestic Energy Micro-gener
 ation (Jacky BOURGEOIS) [MODIFIÉ]</td></tr>\n<tr><th align=left>Organisateur
 :</th><td>"Benoit Combemale" &lt\;benoit.combemale@irisa.fr&gt\; </td></tr>\
 n</table>\n<p>\n<table border='0'>\n<tr><th align=left>Endroit :</th><td>"Re
 nnes-Salle Lipari (F202)" &lt\;rennes-salle_lipari@zimbra-local.inria.fr&gt\
 ; </td></tr>\n<tr><th align=left>Ressources :</th><td>"Rennes-Salle Lipari (
 F202)" &lt\;rennes-salle_lipari@zimbra-local.inria.fr&gt\; (Rennes-Salle Lip
 ari (F202)) </td></tr>\n<tr><th align=left>Heure:</th><td>Mardi 13 Novembre 
 2012\, 13:00:00 - 14:00:00 GMT +01:00 Bruxelles\, Copenhague\, Madrid\, Pari
 s\n </td></tr></table>\n<p>\n<table border='0'>\n<tr><th align=left>Invités:
 </th><td>erwan.bousse@irisa.fr\; mathieu.acher@irisa.fr\; martin.faunes_carv
 allo@inria.fr\; dionysios.efstathiou@irisa.fr\; phillipa.bennett@inria.fr\; 
 fabio.buiati@irisa.fr\; marco.biazzini@inria.fr\; ivan.paez_anaya@irisa.fr\;
  erwan.bousse@gmail.com\; antonio-junior.mattos@irisa.fr\; an.phungkhac@inri
 a.fr ... </td></tr>\n</table>\n<div>*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*</div><br>Abstract: D
 istributed micro-generation is considered one of the cornerstones of the fut
 ure energy infrastructure and residential energy generation using solar pane
 ls\, heat pumps\, etc. has become a feasible option for most homeowners. Yet
  practical savings fall far short of this target for three reasons: (a) resi
 dential energy production and consumption are out of sync\, (b) the practice
  of turning self-generated energy into money via feed-in tariffs essentially
  makes energy production invisible (c) and the available of seemingly free e
 nergy (after investment) undermines attempts to use feedback mechanisms to c
 hange people's energy behaviour in a positive way. Past research has focused
  on energy demand reduction\, looking at the technological\, human and socia
 l issues. In contrast\, energy generation has not yet been a focus of invest
 igation in computing and human computer interaction research. My research wi
 ll investigate energy demand shifting to help consumers narrow the gap betwe
 en the amount of energy they produce and the amount of energy they generate 
 by answering the research question: Is the combination of accurate algorithm
 s and useful HCIs an effective way to synchronize energy micro-generation an
 d energy consumption while maintaining user comfort and user acceptability i
 n residential context?</body></html>
LOCATION:"Rennes-Salle Lipari (F202)" <rennes-salle_lipari@zimbra-local.inri
 a.fr>
