BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:0b7a0bdc-b50e-4a8d-a3e8-550b15dfaa50
SUMMARY:DiverSE Coffee : Ludovic Mouline
DESCRIPTION:Hi all\, \n\nWe are happy to have Ludovic Mouline as a guest spe
 aker for our next DiverSE Coffee. \nHe will be presenting his latest accepte
 d paper on "Enabling Temporal-Aware Contexts for Adaptative Distributed Syst
 ems". \nThis work will be presented at ACM SAC track on Software Architectur
 e: Theory\, Technology\, and Applications. \n\nEnters Ludovic: \n"Distribute
 d adaptive systems are composed of federated entities offering remote inspec
 tion and reconfiguration abilities. This is often realized using a MAPE-K lo
 op\, which constantly evaluates system and environment parameters and derive
 s corrective actions\, if necessary. \nThe OpenStack Watcher project uses su
 ch a loop to implement resource optimization services for multi-tenant cloud
 s. To ensure a timely reaction in the event of failures\, the MAPE-K loop is
  executed with a high frequency. \nA major drawback of such reactivity is th
 at many actions\, e.g.\, the migration of containers in the cloud\, take mor
 e time to be effective and their effects to be measurable than the MAPE-k lo
 op execution frequency. \nUnfinished actions\, as well as their expected eff
 ects over time\, are not taken into consideration in MAPE-K loop processes\,
  leading upcoming analysis phases potentially take sub-optimal actions. \nIn
  this paper\, we propose an extended context representation for MAPE-K loop 
 that integrates the history of planned actions as well as their expected eff
 ects over time into the context representations. \nThis information can then
  be used during the upcoming analysis and planing phases to compare measured
  and expected context metrics. \nWe demonstrate on a cloud elasticity manage
 r case study that such temporal action-aware context leads to improved reaso
 ners while still be highly scalable." \n\nThe presentation is held this Thur
 sday in room Minquiers at 1 p.m. \n\nKind regards\,
LOCATION:"Rennes-Salle Minquiers (B025)" <rennes-salle_minquiers@zimbra-loca
 l.inria.fr>
ATTENDEE;CN=Ludovic Mouline;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=ACCEPTED:mailto:lu
 dovic.mouline@irisa.fr
ATTENDEE;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=NEEDS-ACTION;RSVP=TRUE:mailto:diverse
 @inria.fr
ATTENDEE;CN=Rennes-Salle Minquiers (B025);CUTYPE=RESOURCE;ROLE=NON-PARTICIPA
 NT;PARTSTAT=ACCEPTED:mailto:rennes-salle_minquiers@zimbra-local.inria.fr
X-MOZ-LASTACK:20180417T122343Z
X-MOZ-GENERATION:1
ORGANIZER;CN=Amine Benelallam:mailto:amine.benelallam@inria.fr
