BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:0bc5b763-1cec-420d-a549-2e4f89a812fb
SUMMARY:[seminar] Enabling application development for the Internet of Thing
 s: Programming Abstractions and Middleware
DESCRIPTION:A. Pathak\, from the Arles team in Rocquencourt will visit us on
  Friday and will give a talk about his work in the area of IoT \nThe talk wi
 ll be in Minquiers \n\nApplication development in the Internet of Things (Io
 T) is challenging because it involves dealing with a wide range of related i
 ssues such as lack of separation of concerns\, lack of high level of abstrac
 tions to address the large scale and heterogeneity in IoT applications\, and
  a significant amount of code that needs to be written for matching the char
 acteristics of a given domain. Several approaches have been proposed in the 
 closely related field of wireless sensor network and pervasive computing to 
 address the above challenges in a general case. However\, existing approache
 s for IoT application development only cover limited subsets of above mentio
 ned challenges. \n\nIn this presentation\, we cover the recent work at the A
 RLES project-team on enabling application development for the IoT\, starting
  with a probabilistic approach to registration of mobile sensing devices\, d
 esigned to address the issue of large scale. Then\, we present our work on S
 rijan\, a development approach that extends concepts from sensor networking 
 to provide a multi-stage model-driven approach separating the problem of dev
 eloping an IoT application into different parts corresponding to the various
  stakeholders involved in the process\, providing each of them with a custom
 ized set of abstractions. 
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<html><body><h3>La réunion suivante a été modif
 iée :</h3>\n\n<p>\n<table border='0'>\n<tr><th align=left>Sujet :</th><td>[s
 eminar] Enabling application development for the Internet of Things: Program
 ming Abstractions and Middleware </td></tr>\n<tr><th align=left>Organisateur
 :</th><td>"Benoit Baudry" &lt\;benoit.baudry@inria.fr&gt\; </td></tr>\n</tab
 le>\n<p>\n<table border='0'>\n<tr><th align=left>Heure:</th><td>Vendredi 27 
 Septembre 2013\, 14:00:00 - 15:00:00 GMT +01:00 Bruxelles\, Copenhague\, Mad
 rid\, Paris\n </td></tr></table>\n<p>\n<table border='0'>\n<tr><th align=lef
 t>Invités:</th><td>france@CS.ColoState.EDU\; edward-mauricio.alferez-salinas
 @inria.fr\; walter.rudametkin-ivey@inria.fr\; andre.elie@inria.fr\; simon.al
 lier@inria.fr\; maxime.tricoire@irisa.fr\; guillaume.becan@inria.fr\; vincen
 t.fontanella@inria.fr\; fabien.coulon@inria.fr\; sana.ben-nasr@inria.fr\; fr
 ancisco.acosta@inria.fr ... </td></tr>\n</table>\n<div>*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*</
 div><br>A. Pathak\, from the Arles team in Rocquencourt will visit us on Fri
 day and will give a talk about his work in the area of IoT <br>The talk will
  be in Minquiers <br><br>Application development in the Internet of Things (
 IoT) is challenging because it involves dealing with a wide range of related
  issues such as lack of separation of concerns\, lack of high level of abstr
 actions to address the large scale and heterogeneity in IoT applications\, a
 nd a significant amount of code that needs to be written for matching the ch
 aracteristics of a given domain. Several approaches have been proposed in th
 e closely related field of wireless sensor network and pervasive computing t
 o address the above challenges in a general case. However\, existing approac
 hes for IoT application development only cover limited subsets of above ment
 ioned challenges. <br><br>In this presentation\, we cover the recent work at
  the ARLES project-team on enabling application development for the IoT\, st
 arting with a probabilistic approach to registration of mobile sensing devic
 es\, designed to address the issue of large scale. Then\, we present our wor
 k on Srijan\, a development approach that extends concepts from sensor netwo
 rking to provide a multi-stage model-driven approach separating the problem 
 of developing an IoT application into different parts corresponding to the v
 arious stakeholders involved in the process\, providing each of them with a 
 customized set of abstractions. </body></html>
