BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:0d64a8c5-5c4c-49f7-8d79-e52f9077874c
SUMMARY:DiverSE Coffee
DESCRIPTION:Hi all\, \n\nWe're happy to have Dorian tomorrow as our next Div
 erSE Coffee speaker.\n\nEnters @Dorian: Executable Domain-Specific Languages
  (DSLs) enable the execution of behavioral models. While an execution is mos
 tly driven by the model content (e.g. control structures)\, many use cases r
 equire interacting with the running model\, such as simulating scenarios in 
 an automated or interactive way\, or coupling the model with other models of
  the system or environment. The management of these interactions is usually 
 hardcoded into the semantics of the DSL\, which prevents its reuse for other
  DSLs and the provision of generic tools (e.g. interactive debugger). In thi
 s paper\, we propose a metalanguage for complementing the definition of exec
 utable DSLs with explicit behavioral interfaces to enable external tools to 
 interact with executed models in a unified way. We implemented the proposed 
 metalanguage in the GEMOC Studio\, and show how behavioral interfaces enable
  the realization of tools that are generic\, and thus\, usable for different
  executable DSLs.\n\nThe presentation is held this Thursday\, April 11th in 
 room Minquiers at 1 pm.\n\nKind regards\,\nJuliana.
LOCATION:"Rennes-Salle Minquiers (B025\, Vidéoprojecteur )" <rennes-salle_mi
 nquiers@zimbra-local.inria.fr>
ATTENDEE;CN=juliana alves-pereira;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=NEEDS-ACTION
 ;RSVP=TRUE:mailto:juliana.alves-pereira@irisa.fr
ATTENDEE;CN=diverse;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=NEEDS-ACTION;RSVP=TRUE:mai
 lto:diverse@inria.fr
ATTENDEE;CN=Dorian Leroy;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=NEEDS-ACTION;RSVP=TRU
 E:mailto:dorian.leroy@irisa.fr
ATTENDEE;CN="Rennes-Salle Minquiers (B025, Vidéoprojecteur )";CUTYPE=RESOURC
 E;ROLE=NON-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=ACCEPTED:mailto:rennes-salle_minquiers@zimbr
 a-local.inria.fr
ORGANIZER;CN=Juliana Alves pereira:mailto:juliana.alves-pereira@irisa.fr
