BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:14c92c95-0729-463b-b30b-d8cb6818a83e
SUMMARY:[SEMINAR] Mobility Information Management in Pervasive Environments 
 (Fábio Buiati)
DESCRIPTION:Title: Mobility Information Management in Pervasive Environments
 \n\nAbstract:In the Future Mobile Internet\, one of the most challenging asp
 ects is to discover the available neighbor access networks\, it’s characteri
 stics and services as the user moves. This presentation addresses a general 
 approach towards the deployment of a Mobility Information Service management
  infrastructure in a pervasive and heterogeneous environment.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<html><body><h3>Nouvelle demande de réunion ci-
 dessous :</h3>\n\n<p>\n<table border='0'>\n<tr><th align=left>Sujet :</th><t
 d>[SEMINAR] Mobility Information Management in Pervasive Environments (Fábio
  Buiati) </td></tr>\n<tr><th align=left>Organisateur:</th><td>"Benoit Combem
 ale" &lt\;benoit.combemale@irisa.fr&gt\; </td></tr>\n</table>\n<p>\n<table b
 order='0'>\n<tr><th align=left>Endroit :</th><td>"Rennes-Salle Lipari (F202)
 " &lt\;rennes-salle_lipari@zimbra-local.inria.fr&gt\; </td></tr>\n<tr><th al
 ign=left>Ressources :</th><td>"Rennes-Salle Lipari (F202)" &lt\;rennes-salle
 _lipari@zimbra-local.inria.fr&gt\; (Lieu : Rennes\, Bâtiment : F\, Étage : o
 range\, Salle : F202) </td></tr>\n<tr><th align=left>Heure:</th><td>Jeudi 14
  Juin 2012\, 13:00:00 - 14:00:00 GMT +01:00 Bruxelles\, Copenhague\, Madrid\
 , Paris\n </td></tr></table>\n<p>\n<table border='0'>\n<tr><th align=left>In
 vités:</th><td>marco.biazzini@inria.fr\; ivan.paez_anaya@irisa.fr\; erwan.bo
 usse@gmail.com\; antonio-junior.mattos@irisa.fr\; an.phungkhac@inria.fr\; ju
 lien.richard-foy@irisa.fr\; joao.ferreira_filho@inria.fr\; suresh.pillay@iri
 sa.fr\; jean-emile.dartois@inria.fr\; jonathan.yves.marchand@irisa.fr\; xavi
 er.dolques@inria.fr ... </td></tr>\n</table>\n<div>*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*</div>
 <br>Title: Mobility Information Management in Pervasive Environments<br><br>
 Abstract:In the Future Mobile Internet\, one of the most challenging aspects
  is to discover the available neighbor access networks\, it’s characteristic
 s and services as the user moves. This presentation addresses a general appr
 oach towards the deployment of a Mobility Information Service management inf
 rastructure in a pervasive and heterogeneous environment.</body></html>
