BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:17e9c495-df4e-40db-a8cf-a9c3b0326c68
SUMMARY:DiverSE Coffee: Eduardo Silva
DESCRIPTION:Hi all\, \n\nWe are happy to receive Eduardo Silva as a guest sp
 eaker for our next DiverSE Coffee. \n\nEduardo is a Ph.D. student at the Fed
 eral University of Rio Grande do Norte\, with a co-guardianship period in "U
 niversité de Bretagne Sud"\, IUT de Vannes. He holds a bachelor degree in Co
 mputer Science from the Federal University of Rio Grande do Norte (2012) and
  a Masters in Systems and Computation from the Federal University of Rio Gra
 nde do Norte (2015). He currently works in the Systems-of-Systems area\, wit
 h an emphasis on aspects related to software architecture design and simulat
 ion of these systems. \n\nEduardo will be presenting his work on "Using GEMO
 C and PLASMA Lab for Architectural Verification". \n\nEnters Eduardo: \n\n" 
 Among the activities of Systems-of-Systems modeling\, the software architect
 ure plays a key role by defining the constituent parts and the means they ha
 ve to cooperate. However\, the inner dynamism of this kind of system hampers
  the whole modeling process and adds uncertainty to the models. To mitigate 
 this problem\, possible alternatives including simulation of models to fores
 ee what might happen in a " deploy " environment and model-checking the arch
 itectures for predefined properties. To do so\, it is fundamental to use des
 ign mechanisms that support the uncertainty and dynamism that shall be simul
 ated and verified. \nIn this context\, SosADL was defined as an architectura
 l description language that supports a detailed\, formal modeling of systems
 -of-systems. The language is being developed by ArchWare team and encompasse
 s a set of tools from modeling to generation of end-user artifacts. Among th
 e currently under-development tools\, there is a GEMOC-based execution envir
 onment that will enable the simulation of SosADL models. On the other hand\,
  PLASMA Lab emerges as a powerful statistical model checker\, already with s
 ome proposals of integration with SosADL. \n\nThis talk is about joining the
  two worlds together: simulation and verification\, using the execution envi
 ronment to support the statistical model checker and to allow the end-user t
 o both observe the execution and verify a set of properties within an archit
 ecture." \n\n\nThe presentation is held in Minquiers\, Thursday 30th at 1 p.
 m. \n\n\nKind regards\, \n\n\n\n
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<html><body id='htmlmode'><h3>The following mee
 ting has been modified:</h3>\n\n<p>\n<table border='0'>\n<tr><th align=left>
 Subject:</th><td>DiverSE Coffee: Eduardo Silva [MODIFIED]</td></tr>\n<tr><th
  align=left>Organiser:</th><td>"Amine Benelallam" &lt\;amine.benelallam@inri
 a.fr&gt\; </td></tr>\n</table>\n<p>\n<table border='0'>\n<tr><th align=left>
 Location:</th><td>"Rennes-Salle Minquiers (B025)" &lt\;rennes-salle_minquier
 s@zimbra-local.inria.fr&gt\; </td></tr>\n<tr><th align=left>Resources:</th><
 td>"Rennes-Salle Minquiers (B025)" &lt\;rennes-salle_minquiers@zimbra-local.
 inria.fr&gt\; (Rennes-Salle Minquiers (B025)) </td></tr>\n<tr><th align=left
 >Time:</th><td>Thursday\, 30 November\, 2017\, 1:00:00 PM - 2:00:00 PM GMT +
 01:00 Brussels\, Copenhagen\, Madrid\, Paris\n </td></tr></table>\n<p>\n<tab
 le border='0'>\n<tr><th align=left>Invitees:</th><td>amine.benelallam@inria.
 fr\; diverse@inria.fr\; eduardo-alexandre.ferreira-silva@irisa.fr </td></tr>
 \n</table>\n<div>*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*</div><br><div style="font-family: times
  new roman\, new york\, times\, serif\; font-size: 12pt\; color: #000000"><d
 iv style="font-family: times new roman\, new york\, times\, serif\; font-siz
 e: 12pt\; color: #000000" data-mce-style="font-family: times new roman\, new
  york\, times\, serif\; font-size: 12pt\; color: #000000\;"><div style="font
 -family: times new roman\, new york\, times\, serif\; font-size: 12pt\; colo
 r: #000000" data-mce-style="font-family: times new roman\, new york\, times\
 , serif\; font-size: 12pt\; color: #000000\;"><div style="font-family: times
  new roman\, new york\, times\, serif\; font-size: 12pt\; color: #000000" da
 ta-mce-style="font-family: times new roman\, new york\, times\, serif\; font
 -size: 12pt\; color: #000000\;"><div>Hi all\,&nbsp\;<br></div><div><br></div
 ><div>We are happy to receive Eduardo Silva as a guest speaker for our next 
 DiverSE Coffee.</div><div><br></div><div>Eduardo is a Ph.D. student at the F
 ederal University of Rio Grande do Norte\, with a co-guardianship period in 
 "Université de Bretagne Sud"\, IUT de Vannes. He holds a bachelor degree in 
 Computer Science from the Federal University of Rio Grande do Norte (2012) a
 nd a Masters in Systems and Computation from the Federal University of Rio G
 rande do Norte (2015). He currently works in the Systems-of-Systems area\, w
 ith an emphasis on aspects related to software architecture design and simul
 ation of these systems.</div><div><br></div><div>Eduardo will be presenting 
 his work on "Using GEMOC and PLASMA Lab for Architectural Verification".<br>
 </div><div><br></div><div>Enters Eduardo:&nbsp\;</div><div><br></div><div>"<
 span style="font-size: 12pt\;">Among the activities of Systems-of-Systems mo
 deling\, the software architecture plays a key role by defining the constitu
 ent parts and the means they have to cooperate. However\, the inner dynamism
  of this kind of system hampers the whole modeling process and adds </span>u
 ncertainty<span style="font-size: 12pt\;"> to the models. To mitigate this p
 roblem\, possible alternatives </span>including<span style="font-size: 12pt\
 ;">&nbsp\;simulation of models to foresee what might happen in a "</span>dep
 loy<span style="font-size: 12pt\;">" environment and model-checking the arch
 itectures for predefined properties. To do so\, it is fundamental to use des
 ign mechanisms that </span>support<span style="font-size: 12pt\;">&nbsp\;the
  uncertainty and dynamism that shall be simulated and verified.</span><p sty
 le="margin: 0px\;" data-mce-style="margin: 0px\;">In this context\, SosADL w
 as defined as an architectural description language that supports a detailed
 \, formal modeling of systems-of-systems. The language is being developed by
  ArchWare team and encompasses a set of tools from modeling to generation of
  end-user artifacts. Among the currently under-development tools\, there is 
 a GEMOC-based execution environment that will enable the simulation of SosAD
 L models. On the other hand\, PLASMA Lab emerges as a powerful statistical m
 odel checker\, already with some proposals of integration with SosADL.<br> <
 br>This talk is about joining the two worlds together: simulation and verifi
 cation\, using the execution environment to support the statistical model ch
 ecker and to allow the end-user to both observe the execution and verify a s
 et of properties within an architecture."</p><p style="margin: 0px\;" data-m
 ce-style="margin: 0px\;"><br></p><p style="margin: 0px\;" data-mce-style="ma
 rgin: 0px\;">The presentation&nbsp\;is held in Minquiers\, Thursday 30th at 
 1 p.m.</p><p style="margin: 0px\;" data-mce-style="margin: 0px\;"><br></p><p
  style="margin: 0px\;" data-mce-style="margin: 0px\;">Kind regards\,</p></di
 v><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div></div></div></div></div></bod
 y></html>
