BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:20091008T122152Z-734f5-2ee0-4bf6410a-Oracle
SUMMARY:[O][SEMINAR] Good Practices as a Modeling Assistant (Vincent Legloah
 ec)
DESCRIPTION:To preserve their knowledge\, companies often define good practi
 ces that must be respected. This also applies to the modeling stage in a sof
 tware development lifecycle. However\, the checking of compliance with good 
 practices is often do in posteriori\, which generates a waste of time and th
 erefore of money. This is due to the lack of tools to exploit them at modeli
 ng stage. This paper tackles the problem by focusing on the definition and t
 he enactment of good modeling practices. Based on several hundred of the wel
 l known good modeling practices\, we identified the required properties of a
  description language. We propose a such language by using a formalism which
  is independent of any tool. We present an example of its implementation in 
 an Eclipse modeling editor. As a case study\, we show how to apply our appro
 ach on several examples of good modeling practices including an industrial c
 ase.
LOCATION:Rennes-Salle Lipari F202 (F ora
