BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:20091012T113019Z-73713-2ee0-14cab3d9-Oracle
SUMMARY:[O][SEMINAR] Getting meaning from your data (Freddy Munoz)
DESCRIPTION:Nowadays we obtain raw data from different sources such as surve
 ys\, historical measures\, experiments\, and so on. This data is nonetheless
  nothing more than ordered scalar or decimal values\, counting\, and propert
 ies. Alone\, it can't answer our questions\, back our assumptions\, or satis
 fy our need – it is "meaningless". Answers come after detailed and careful d
 epuration and analysis. R is a piece of software that supports such analysis
  and helps us getting the answers and the meaning we need from our data. \n\
 nThis talk is not an R tutorial\, but rather about what R can do for you to 
 get the hidden meaning from your raw material. 
LOCATION:Lipari
