BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:20100217T101928Z-7b5c0-2ee0-3b0ee3b0-Oracle
SUMMARY:[O][SEMINAR] Assessing Decision Making for Self-Adaptive Systems (Fr
 eddy Munoz)
DESCRIPTION:abstract: Self-adaptive systems can provide effective assistance
  in a large number of human activities. This is due to their ability at auto
 matically reasoning on a large number of factors to propose effective adapta
 tion decisions. However\, these systems will fully deliver their promises on
 ly if system designers can ensure the effectiveness of decisions in all poss
 ible situations. This requires robust techniques for assessing that the reas
 oning process implemented in such systems is correct. In this talk I present
  multi-dimensional covering arrays (MDCA) for sampling all possible environm
 ent conditions that can affect the decision making process. MDCA specificall
 y target environments that can trigger complex decisions by explicitly intro
 ducing the notion of history in the environment sampling. \n\nKeywords: comb
 inatorial interaction testing\, self-adaptive systems\, decision making asse
 ssment.
LOCATION:Rennes-Salle Lipari F202 (F ora
ATTENDEE;CN=Aymeric HERVIEU;CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;PARTSTAT=NEEDS-ACTION;RSVP=TRU
 E;X-ORACLE-SHOWASFREE=FREE;X-ORACLE-GUID=71FE9B46D6EF9191E040608A0112030A:ma
