BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:20100309T072111Z-7c4fc-2ee0-27f2356d-Oracle
SUMMARY:[O]Séminaire Hidehiko Masuhara
DESCRIPTION:Title: Aspect-oriented programming is also for abstracting modul
 e\n      boundaries\n\nAbstract:\n\nWhile aspect-oriented programming (AOP) 
 has been recognized as\ntechniques for modularizing crosscutting concerns\, 
 this view is\nsometimes confusing when characterizing essentials of the para
 digm and\nwhen comparing with other paradigms and languages.  In this talk\,
  we\npropose an additional view\, where AOP contributed more to abstracting\
 nmodule boundaries with respect to the Parnas' modularization\nprinciple.  W
 e discuss whether the view can accurately explain\nexisting AOP and non-AOP 
 techniques\, and future directions of\nmodularity studies.\n\n
LOCATION:Salle Oleron visio depuis Nantes
ATTENDEE;CN=Aymeric HERVIEU;CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;PARTSTAT=ACCEPTED;X-ORACLE-SHO
 WASFREE=BUSY;X-ORACLE-GUID=71FE9B46D6EF9191E040608A0112030A:mailto:Aymeric.H
 ervieu@irisa.fr
