BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:20100409T161355Z-0000116900002ee00000336200002ee0-OCDC-Oracle
SUMMARY:[O][SEMINAR] Threats to validity in experimental validation: why? ho
 w? where? (Freddy Munoz)
DESCRIPTION:abstract: Nowadays\, many research work require experimental val
 idation over empirical data. Such experimental validation implies collecting
  experimental subjects\, making a set of assumptions and decision\, measurin
 g\, and analyzing data. Each of these phases introduce what in literature ar
 e called "threats to validity"\, or deviations that can hamper the validity 
 of the conclusions we draw from empirical results. In this talk I present wh
 at are those infamous threats to validity\, how\, where\, and why is it impo
 rtant to consider and include them in your research.\n\nkeywords: experiment
 al assessment\, threats to validity\, empirical studies.
