BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:20100602T165348Z-8192b-2ee0-56fe6a8a-Oracle
SUMMARY:[O][SEMINAR] Security-Driven Model-Based Dynamic Adaptation (Tejeddi
 ne Mouelhi)
DESCRIPTION:Security is a key-challenge for software engineering\, especiall
 y \nwhen considering access control and software evolutions.\nNo satisfying 
 solution exists for maintaining the alignment\nof access control policies wi
 th the business logic. Current\nimplementations of access control rely on th
 e separation\nbetween the policy and the application code. In practice\,\nth
 is separation is not so strict and some rules are hardcoded\nwithin the appl
 ication\, making the evolution of the\npolicy difficult. We propose a new me
 thodology for implementing\nsecurity-driven applications. From a policy defi
 ned\nby a security expert\, we generate an architectural model\, \nreflectin
 g the access control policy. We leverage the advances\nin the models@runtime
  domain to keep this model synchronized\nwith the running system. When the p
 olicy is updated\,\nthe architectural model is updated\, which in turn recon
 figures\nthe running system. As a proof of concept\, we apply\nthe approach 
 to the development of a library management\nsystem.
LOCATION:Rennes-Salle Lipari F202 (F ora
