BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:202f8756-f0cc-46b3-97ba-2bf34f6e5a2a
SUMMARY:[SEMINAR] DEPENDABILITY DRIVEN MANAGEMENT IN SMART BUILDINGS (H. Hao
 uas)
DESCRIPTION:\n\n\nThe recent convergence of pervasive computing and service 
 oriented approaches has caused interest in the development of smart environm
 ents being employed for valuable functions such as home health monitoring. T
 he emerging complexity in these autonomic systems\, services and application
 s has raised unprecedented challenges for system management. These systems a
 re dynamic and fault-prone which makes it necessary to design new techniques
  to ensure their dependabilities. This work focuses on establishing an infra
 structure that enables the continuous evaluation of dependability of an appl
 ication and the overall system in a service-oriented components platform. We
  propose a decentralized architecture for this evaluation. Our architecture 
 allows placing a measure for dependability calculated by aggregating the con
 sumers' evaluations. Our framework also provides means to extend the evaluat
 ion methods to improve the dependability representation. We apply our propos
 al in the context of home automation and we propose an implementation of our
  framework. The implementation uses the component plateform KEVOREE and the 
 Software framework EnTiMid. 
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<html><body><h3>La réunion suivante a été modif
 iée :</h3>\n\n<p>\n<table border='0'>\n<tr><th align=left>Sujet :</th><td>[S
 EMINAR] DEPENDABILITY DRIVEN MANAGEMENT IN SMART BUILDINGS (H. Haouas) [MODI
 FIÉ]</td></tr>\n<tr><th align=left>Organisateur:</th><td>"Benoit Combemale" 
 &lt\;benoit.combemale@irisa.fr&gt\; </td></tr>\n</table>\n<p>\n<table border
 ='0'>\n<tr><th align=left>Endroit :</th><td>Rennes-Salle Lipari (F202) </td>
 </tr>\n<tr><th align=left>Ressources :</th><td>Rennes-Salle Lipari (F202) (L
 ieu : Rennes\, Bâtiment : F\, Étage : orange\, Salle : F202) </td></tr>\n<tr
 ><th align=left>Heure:</th><td>Vendredi 7 Octobre 2011\, 13:00:00 - 14:00:00
  GMT +01:00 Bruxelles\, Copenhague\, Madrid\, Paris\n </td></tr></table>\n<p
 >\n<table border='0'>\n<tr><th align=left>Invités:</th><td>triskell@irisa.fr
 \; triskell-all@irisa.fr\; "Johann Bourcier" <johann.bourcier@inria.fr>\; "X
 avier Dolques" <xavier.dolques@inria.fr>\; "Clement Guy" <clement.guy@inria.
 fr>\; "Viet-Hoa Nguyen" <viet-hoa.nguyen@inria.fr>\; "Hanen Haouas" <hanen.h
 aouas@inria.fr>\; "Didier Vojtisek" <didier.vojtisek@inria.fr>\; "Olivier-Na
 thanael Ben_david" <olivier-nathanael.ben_david@inria.fr> </td></tr>\n</tabl
 e>\n<div>*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*</div><br><div style='font-family:Times New Roma
 n\; font-size: 12pt\; color: #000000\;'><div style="font-family:Times New Ro
 man\; font-size: 12pt\; color: #000000\;">\n\n\n\n\n\n<p><span style="font-s
 ize: 12.000000pt\; font-family: 'Times New Roman'">The recent convergence of
  pervasive computing and service oriented approaches has caused\ninterest in
  the development of smart environments being employed for valuable functions
  such as\nhome health monitoring. The emerging complexity in these autonomic
  systems\, services and\napplications has raised unprecedented challenges fo
 r system management. These systems are\ndynamic and fault-prone which makes 
 it necessary to design new techniques to ensure their\ndependabilities. This
  work focuses on establishing an infrastructure that enables the continuous\
 nevaluation of dependability of an application and the overall system in a s
 ervice-oriented\ncomponents platform. We propose a decentralized architectur
 e for this evaluation. Our\narchitecture allows placing a measure for depend
 ability calculated by aggregating the consumers'\nevaluations. Our framework
  also provides means to extend the evaluation methods to improve the\ndepend
 ability representation. We apply our proposal in the context of home automat
 ion and we\npropose an implementation of our framework. The implementation u
 ses the component plateform\nKEVOREE and the Software framework EnTiMid.\n</
 span></p>\n</div></div></body></html>
LOCATION:Rennes-Salle Lipari (F202)
