BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:2db9f8f1-8ba8-4c77-936c-0bc6704c0ac3
SUMMARY:DiverSE Coffee [Mohamed GRAIET]: A formal approach for the verificat
 ion of software composition
DESCRIPTION:Hi all\, \n\nWe're happy to host a DiverSE Coffee this Thursday 
 starring Mohamed GRAIET\, an assistant associate professor at ENSAI.\nMohame
 d will be presenting his work on the verification of software composition us
 ing the Event-B Method.\n \nEnters Mohamed:\n"Reuse is a key concept in buil
 ding software systems. It enables the composition of a set of existing softw
 are to build new ones\, with added value. In the context of our work\, we ar
 e interested in the composition of two types of software\, namely Web servic
 es and free software based on FOSS (Free and Open Source Software) packages.
 \n\nDespite the research efforts devoted to verification of the correctness 
 Web services and FOSS composition\, it remains one of the most difficult tas
 ks. A composite service is said to be correct if it meets a set of requireme
 nts of two types: QoS and Transactional requirements. QoS requirements are d
 efined by means of a service-level agreement (SLA)\, coming in the form of Q
 oS constraints. Whilst\, transactional requirements are specified by designe
 rs using the concept of Accepted Termination States (ETAs). Finally\, A FOSS
  composite software is said to be correct if it respects a set of constraint
 s on dependencies and capacities.\n\nTo solve this verification problem\, we
  propose a formal approach based on the Event-B method. This approach can be
  summed up in two points:\n     i)  Event-B formalization of service composi
 tion with Event-B.\n     ii) Event-B formalization of FOSS software composit
 ion in a cloud context.\n\nIn this talk\, I'll present the proposed approach
  and elaborate on the different steps involved in the verification process\,
  from formalization to proof."\n\nAn extended abstract in French can also be
  found below.\n\nThis presentation is held in Minquiers at 1 pm.\n\nRegards\
 ,\n
LOCATION:"Rennes-Salle Minquiers (B025\, Vidéoprojecteur )" <rennes-salle_mi
 nquiers@zimbra-local.inria.fr>
ATTENDEE;CN=mohamed graiet;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=NEEDS-ACTION;RSVP=T
 RUE:mailto:mohamed.graiet@ensai.fr
ATTENDEE;CN=Olivier Barais;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=NEEDS-ACTION;RSVP=T
 RUE:mailto:olivier.barais@irisa.fr
