UID:2fc2fa2c-188e-4280-b4bf-89035d3223da
SUMMARY:[SEMINAR] Complex patterns in P2P function optimization and (possibl
 y) in ESE (Marco Biazzini)
DESCRIPTION:I will present some relevant notions and discoveries in the doma
 in of complex systems and how they relate to my research about P2P function 
 optimization. Then I'll give an outline on how complex patterns could be use
 ful to describe the organization and the evolution of Software Projects.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<html><body><h3>Nouvelle demande de réunion ci-
 dessous :</h3>\n\n<p>\n<table border='0'>\n<tr><th align=left>Sujet :</th><t
 d>[SEMINAR] Complex patterns in P2P function optimization and (possibly) in 
 ESE (Marco Biazzini) </td></tr>\n<tr><th align=left>Organisateur:</th><td>"B
 enoit Combemale" &lt\;benoit.combemale@irisa.fr&gt\; </td></tr>\n</table>\n<
 p>\n<table border='0'>\n<tr><th align=left>Endroit :</th><td>"Rennes-Salle L
 ipari (F202)" &lt\;rennes-salle_lipari@zimbra-local.inria.fr&gt\; </td></tr>
 \n<tr><th align=left>Ressources :</th><td>"Rennes-Salle Lipari (F202)" &lt\;
 rennes-salle_lipari@zimbra-local.inria.fr&gt\; (Lieu : Rennes\, Bâtiment : F
 \, Étage : orange\, Salle : F202) </td></tr>\n<tr><th align=left>Heure:</th>
 <td>Lundi 25 Juin 2012\, 13:00:00 - 14:00:00 GMT +01:00 Bruxelles\, Copenhag
 ue\, Madrid\, Paris\n </td></tr></table>\n<p>\n<table border='0'>\n<tr><th a
 lign=left>Invités:</th><td>marco.biazzini@inria.fr\; ivan.paez_anaya@irisa.f
 r\; erwan.bousse@gmail.com\; antonio-junior.mattos@irisa.fr\; an.phungkhac@i
 nria.fr\; julien.richard-foy@irisa.fr\; joao.ferreira_filho@inria.fr\; sures
 h.pillay@irisa.fr\; jean-emile.dartois@inria.fr\; jonathan.yves.marchand@iri
 sa.fr\; xavier.dolques@inria.fr ... </td></tr>\n</table>\n<div>*~*~*~*~*~*~*
 ~*~*~*</div><br>I will present some relevant notions and discoveries in the 
 domain of complex systems and how they relate to my research about P2P funct
 ion optimization. Then I'll give an outline on how complex patterns could be
  useful to describe the organization and the evolution of Software Projects.
 </body></html>
