BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:337bc81d-0933-447b-824e-08a9c76231c8
SUMMARY:[SEMINAR] Network Information and Computer Security Lab: A Research 
 Overview
DESCRIPTION:Abstract:\n\nThe NICS Lab is an international leading Security r
 esearch group led by Javier Lopez\, Full Professor of the Computer Science D
 epartment at University of Malaga. NICS is composed of 20 persons\, includin
 g faculty members\, post-doc researchers\, top PhD students\, and technical 
 and management staff. We are involved in a number of research projects as we
 ll as in technology transfer. In this talk I'll give an overview of the diff
 erent research lines we are taking up and the main research projects we part
 icipate in.\n\nShort bio:\n\nDr Carmen Fernández-Gago obtained her PhD in Co
 mputer Science from the University of Liverpool (UK) in 2004. She also worke
 d there on Verification Techniques for non-monodic First-order Temporal Logi
 cs before joining NICS in 2006. She has worked on trust and reputation manag
 ement systems in European projects such as SERENITY\, GREDIA\, SPIKE\, NESSo
 S and recently A4Cloud. She has published many research papers and serves on
  several program committees as well as being involved in the organization of
  conferences in the area of trust management.\n
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<html><body><h3>La réunion suivante a été modif
 iée :</h3>\n\n<p>\n<table border='0'>\n<tr><th align=left>Sujet :</th><td>[S
 EMINAR] Network Information and Computer Security Lab: A Research Overview [
 MODIFIÉ]</td></tr>\n<tr><th align=left>Organisateur:</th><td>"Benoit Baudry"
  &lt\;benoit.baudry@inria.fr&gt\; </td></tr>\n</table>\n<p>\n<table border='
 0'>\n<tr><th align=left>Endroit :</th><td>"Rennes-Salle Crête (F402)" &lt\;r
 ennes-salle_crete@zimbra-local.inria.fr&gt\; </td></tr>\n<tr><th align=left>
 Ressources :</th><td>"Rennes-Salle Crête (F402)" &lt\;rennes-salle_crete@zim
 bra-local.inria.fr&gt\; (Rennes-Salle Crête (F402)) </td></tr>\n<tr><th alig
 n=left>Heure:</th><td>Vendredi 22 Février 2013\, 13:00:00 - 14:00:00 GMT +01
 :00 Bruxelles\, Copenhague\, Madrid\, Paris\n </td></tr></table>\n<p>\n<tabl
 e border='0'>\n<tr><th align=left>Invités:</th><td>francisco.acosta@inria.fr
 \; francisco.moyano@irisa.fr\; sean.sedwards@inria.fr\; louis-marie.traonoue
 z@inria.fr\; cyrille.jegourel@inria.fr\; ulrich.fahrenberg@inria.fr\; benoit
 .delahaye@inria.fr\; kevin.corre@inria.fr\; benoit.boyer@inria.fr\; axel.leg
 ay@inria.fr\; jacky.bourgeois@irisa.fr ... </td></tr>\n</table>\n<div>*~*~*~
 *~*~*~*~*~*~*</div><br>Abstract:<br><br>The NICS Lab is an international lea
 ding Security research group led by Javier Lopez\, Full Professor of the Com
 puter Science Department at University of Malaga. NICS is composed of 20 per
 sons\, including faculty members\, post-doc researchers\, top PhD students\,
  and technical and management staff. We are involved in a number of research
  projects as well as in technology transfer. In this talk I'll give an overv
 iew of the different research lines we are taking up and the main research p
 rojects we participate in.<br><br>Short bio:<br><br>Dr Carmen Fernández-Gago
  obtained her PhD in Computer Science from the University of Liverpool (UK) 
 in 2004. She also worked there on Verification Techniques for non-monodic Fi
 rst-order Temporal Logics before joining NICS in 2006. She has worked on tru
 st and reputation management systems in European projects such as SERENITY\,
  GREDIA\, SPIKE\, NESSoS and recently A4Cloud. She has published many resear
 ch papers and serves on several program committees as well as being involved
  in the organization of conferences in the area of trust management.<br></bo
 dy></html>
LOCATION:"Rennes-Salle Crête (F402)" <rennes-salle_crete@zimbra-local.inria.
 fr>
