BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:3925666f-bd79-4617-b116-bd839ff3307c
SUMMARY:DiverSE Coffee [Manuel Leduc]: Writing fast interpreters on the JVM
DESCRIPTION:Hi all\, \n\nManuel Leduc has kindly accepted our invitation for
  participation in the DiverSE Coffee.\nHe will be sharing his experience on 
 building interpreters on top of the latest JVM.\n\n\nEnters Manuel:\n"Develo
 ping interpreters is a cornerstone of Domain-Specific Languages (DSLs) devel
 opment. Sadly\, performances are often an issue when executing large DSL's p
 rograms.\n\nThe latest virtual machine research done at Oracle labs and impl
 emented in the latest versions of the JVM yield incredible performances boos
 t on interpreted languages implemented on top of the JVM using a mix of Just
 -In-Time (JIT) compiler\, speculative optimization\, partial evaluation and 
 AST annotations.\n\nMy presentation will be a short (~15mns) and (not so) te
 chnical summary of the knowledge I have gathered about Oracle labs research 
 and how I am currently applying them in different contexts.\n\nIn complement
  to the traditional Q&A time following the presentation\, I would like also 
 brainstorm and use your brainpower to think about how we can apply such adva
 nces to the scientific topics of the DiverSE team."\n\nThe presentation is h
 eld in room Minquiers at 1 p.m.\n\nKind regards\,\n\n
LOCATION:"Rennes-Salle Minquiers (B025\, Vidéoprojecteur )" <rennes-salle_mi
 nquiers@zimbra-local.inria.fr>
ATTENDEE;CN=Manuel Leduc;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=ACCEPTED:mailto:manue
 l.leduc@inria.fr
