BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:40b7ce91-e605-4256-a718-ce1d70abf883
SUMMARY:DiverSE Coffee [Caroline Landry] : PitMP\, a Maven plugin to run PiT
 est on multi module projects
DESCRIPTION:Hi all\, \n\nWe are happy to have Caroline Landry as a guest spe
 aker for our next DiverSE Coffee. \nShe will be presenting PitMP\, a tool to
  run PIT test on multi-module maven projects. \n\nEnters Caroline: \n" \nPIT
  is a state of the art mutation testing system\, providing gold standard tes
 t coverage for Java and the JVM. But PIT works on each module independently\
 , and for projects in which tests use classes of others modules\, only a sub
 set of used classes are mutated by PIT. \nThough in such cases\, mutants tha
 t survive the tests placed in the same module could be killed by test cases 
 of other modules. This issue has been around for a while and spotted by the 
 PIT's community several times\, and it was a main issue for Descartes and ST
 AMP. \nSo this talk presents PitMP\, the maven plugin developed to run PiTes
 t on multi-module projects. \n" \n\nThe presentation is held in Markov room 
 at 1 p.m. \n\nCheers\, \n
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<html><body id='htmlmode'><h3>The following is 
 a new meeting request:</h3>\n\n<p>\n<table border='0'>\n<tr><th align=left>S
 ubject:</th><td>DiverSE Coffee [Caroline Landry] : PitMP\, a Maven plugin to
  run PiTest on multi module projects </td></tr>\n<tr><th align=left>Organise
 r:</th><td>"Amine Benelallam" &lt\;amine.benelallam@inria.fr&gt\; </td></tr>
 \n</table>\n<p>\n<table border='0'>\n<tr><th align=left>Time:</th><td>Thursd
 ay\, 1 February\, 2018\, 1:00:00 PM - 2:00:00 PM GMT +01:00 Brussels\, Copen
 hagen\, Madrid\, Paris\n </td></tr></table>\n<p>\n<table border='0'>\n<tr><t
 h align=left>Invitees:</th><td>diverse@inria.fr </td></tr>\n</table>\n<div>*
 ~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*</div><br><div style="font-family: times new roman\, new y
 ork\, times\, serif\; font-size: 12pt\; color: #000000"><div>Hi all\,&nbsp\;
 </div><div><br></div><div>We are happy to have Caroline Landry as a guest sp
 eaker for our next DiverSE Coffee.&nbsp\;</div><div>She will be presenting P
 itMP\, a tool to run PIT test on multi-module maven projects.</div><div><br>
 </div><div>Enters Caroline:&nbsp\;</div><div>"</div><div><div style="font-fa
 mily: 'trebuchet ms'\, sans-serif\; background-color: #ffffff\;" data-mce-st
 yle="font-family: 'trebuchet ms'\, sans-serif\; background-color: #ffffff\;"
 ><span style="font-size: 12pt\;" data-mce-style="font-size: 12pt\;">PIT is a
  state of the art mutation testing system\, providing gold standard test cov
 erage for Java and the JVM. But&nbsp\;</span><span style="font-size: 12pt\;"
  data-mce-style="font-size: 12pt\;">PIT works on each module independently\,
  and for projects in which tests use classes of others modules\,&nbsp\;</spa
 n><span style="font-size: 12pt\;" data-mce-style="font-size: 12pt\;">only a 
 subset of used classes are mutated by PIT.</span></div><div style="font-fami
 ly: 'trebuchet ms'\, sans-serif\; background-color: #ffffff\;" data-mce-styl
 e="font-family: 'trebuchet ms'\, sans-serif\; background-color: #ffffff\;"><
 span style="font-size: 12pt\;" data-mce-style="font-size: 12pt\;">Though in 
 such cases\, mutants that survive the tests placed in the same module could 
 be killed by test cases of other modules. This issue has been around for a w
 hile and spotted by the PIT's community several times\, and it was a main is
 sue for Descartes and STAMP.</span></div><div style="font-family: 'trebuchet
  ms'\, sans-serif\; background-color: #ffffff\;" data-mce-style="font-family
 : 'trebuchet ms'\, sans-serif\; background-color: #ffffff\;"><span style="fo
 nt-size: 12pt\;" data-mce-style="font-size: 12pt\;">So this talk presents Pi
 tMP\, the maven plugin developed&nbsp\;to run PiTest on multi-module project
 s.</span></div>"&nbsp\;</div><div><br></div><div>The presentation is held in
  Markov&nbsp\;room at 1 p.m.</div><div><br></div><div>Cheers\,</div></div></
 body></html>
