BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:549d49bc-0587-4598-bdac-c34299e49ae9
SUMMARY:DiverSE Coffee [Younes Leghouaouta]: MDE for serious games developme
 nt
DESCRIPTION:Hi all\,\n\nPlease welcome Younes LEGHOUAOUTA\, our next DiverSE
  Coffee speaker.\n\nYouness Laghouaouta is a postdoctoral associate at Le Ma
 ns University (LIUM Lab.). \nHe holds an Engineering Diploma from the Nation
 al High School of Computer Science and\nSystems Analysis (Morocco)\, in 2009
 \, and a Ph.D. in Computer Science from the Mohammed V\nUniversity of Rabat 
 (Morocco)\, in 2016. His research interests lie in Model Driven\nEngineering
 . He is particularly interested in model transformation/composition\, model\
 ntraceability\, and co-design.\n\nEnters Younes"\nAs Model Driven Engineerin
 g principles are increasingly applied in the development of\ncomplex softwar
 e\, the use of constraint solving in the specification of model transformati
 ons\nis often required. However\, transformation techniques do not provide f
 ully integrated\nsupports for solving constraints\, and external solvers are
  not well adapted. To deal with this\nissue\, we propose a pattern-matching 
 based approach as a practical solution for enforcing\nconstraints on target 
 models. A transformation infrastructure is semi-automatically\ngenerated and
  it provides support for specifying patterns and producing valid target mode
 ls.\nIn this talk\, I’ll give an overview of the proposed approach and prese
 nt an application\nexample extracted from the Escape’It project. Its objecti
 ve is to develop a serious game to\ntrain the visual skills of children with
  ASD (Autism Syndrome Disorder).\n\nThe presentation is held this Thursday a
 t 1 pm in room Sicile.\n\nRegards\,\n"
LOCATION:"Rennes-Salle Sicile (F302\, Vidéoprojecteur\, Visioconférence\, Au
 dioconférence)" <rennes-salle_sicile@zimbra-local.inria.fr>
ATTENDEE;CN=diverse;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=NEEDS-ACTION;RSVP=TRUE:mai
 lto:diverse@inria.fr
ATTENDEE;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=NEEDS-ACTION;RSVP=TRUE:mailto:youness
 .laghouaouta@univ-lemans.fr
ATTENDEE;CN="Rennes-Salle Sicile (F302, Vidéoprojecteur, Visioconférence, Au
 dioconférence)";CUTYPE=RESOURCE;ROLE=NON-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=ACCEPTED:mailt
 o:rennes-salle_sicile@zimbra-local.inria.fr
ORGANIZER;CN=Amine Benelallam:mailto:amine.benelallam@inria.fr
