BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:558dfd36-4ba5-463a-80e4-ec190a578b0a
SUMMARY:[SEMINAR] Semantic Differences in Model-Driven Engineering (Uli Fahr
 enberg)
DESCRIPTION:\nSyntactic difference between models is a wide research area wi
 th applications in tools for model evolution\, model synchronization and ver
 sion control. On the other hand\, semantic difference between models is rare
 ly discussed. We point out to main use cases of semantic difference between 
 models\, and then propose a categorical framework for defining well-formed d
 ifference operators on model semantics as adjoints of model combinators such
  as conjunction\, disjunction \nand structural composition. We believe that 
 the algebraic theory of semantic difference will allow to define practical m
 odel differencing tools in the future. \n
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<html><body><h3>La réunion suivante a été modif
 iée :</h3>\n\n<p>\n<table border='0'>\n<tr><th align=left>Sujet :</th><td>[S
 EMINAR] Semantic Differences in Model-Driven Engineering (Uli Fahrenberg) [M
 ODIFIÉ]</td></tr>\n<tr><th align=left>Organisateur:</th><td>"Benoit Combemal
 e" &lt\;benoit.combemale@irisa.fr&gt\; </td></tr>\n</table>\n<p>\n<table bor
 der='0'>\n<tr><th align=left>Endroit :</th><td>Rennes-Salle Lipari (F202) </
 td></tr>\n<tr><th align=left>Ressources :</th><td>Rennes-Salle Lipari (F202)
  (Lieu : Rennes\, Bâtiment : F\, Étage : orange\, Salle : F202) </td></tr>\n
 <tr><th align=left>Heure:</th><td>Mardi 4 Octobre 2011\, 13:00:00 - 14:00:00
  GMT +01:00 Bruxelles\, Copenhague\, Madrid\, Paris\n </td></tr></table>\n<p
 >\n<table border='0'>\n<tr><th align=left>Invités:</th><td>triskell@irisa.fr
 \; triskell-all@irisa.fr </td></tr>\n</table>\n<div>*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*</div
 ><br><div style='font-family:Times New Roman\; font-size: 12pt\; color: #000
 000\;'><div style="font-family:Times New Roman\; font-size: 12pt\; color: #0
 00000\;">Syntactic difference between models is a wide research area with ap
 plications in tools for model evolution\, model synchronization and version 
 control. On the other hand\, semantic difference between models is rarely di
 scussed. We point out to main use cases of semantic difference between model
 s\, and then propose a categorical framework for defining well-formed differ
 ence operators on model semantics as adjoints of model combinators such as c
 onjunction\, disjunction<br>and structural composition. We believe that the 
 algebraic theory of semantic difference will allow to define practical model
  differencing tools in the future.<br></div></div></body></html>
LOCATION:Rennes-Salle Lipari (F202)
