BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:67aa1894-9d88-45e2-96c6-4c6aeb7fc30b
SUMMARY:DiverSE Coffee [Gauthier Lyan]: Big data processing and use cases
DESCRIPTION:Hi all\, \n\nWe're happy to have Gauthier Lyan as our next Diver
 SE Coffee speaker. He'll be introducing a couple of frameworks for big data 
 processing and use cases. \n\nIn the Agenda: \n\n- Apache NiFi for Data flow
  integration (with a few examples and use cases) \n- Apache Spark & its arch
 itecture (clustering\, scalability\, limitations) \n- How to use it locally 
 (because it is a genius tool for data engineering\, even for small datasets)
 ? \n- How to simulate a cluster on a computer that has numerous cores and a 
 lot of memory to bypass some local limitations and enhance CPU intensive tas
 ks performance? \n- How to test you data engineering with a framework I made
  for my work? \n\nThe presentation is held next Thursday\, somewhere in the 
 dark side of the lab (Room Bréhat!) at 1 pm. \n\nSee you there! \n\nCheers\,
  \n
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<html><body id='htmlmode'><h3>The following is 
 a new meeting request:</h3>\n\n<p>\n<table border='0'>\n<tr><th align=left>S
 ubject:</th><td>DiverSE Coffee [Gauthier Lyan]: Big data processing and use 
 cases </td></tr>\n<tr><th align=left>Organiser:</th><td>"Amine Benelallam" &
 lt\;amine.benelallam@inria.fr&gt\; </td></tr>\n</table>\n<p>\n<table border=
 '0'>\n<tr><th align=left>Location:</th><td>"Rennes-Salle Bréhat (C001\, Vidé
 oprojecteur\, Visioconférence + Grand écran)" &lt\;rennes-salle_brehat@zimbr
 a-local.inria.fr&gt\; </td></tr>\n<tr><th align=left>Resources:</th><td>"Ren
 nes-Salle Bréhat (C001\, Vidéoprojecteur\, Visioconférence + Grand écran)" &
 lt\;rennes-salle_brehat@zimbra-local.inria.fr&gt\; (Lieu : Rennes\, Bâtiment
  : C\, Étage : jaune\, Salle : C001) </td></tr>\n<tr><th align=left>Time:</t
 h><td>Thursday\, 29 November\, 2018\, 13:00:00 - 14:00:00 GMT +01:00 Brussel
 s\, Copenhagen\, Madrid\, Paris\n </td></tr></table>\n<p>\n<table border='0'
 >\n<tr><th align=left>Invitees:</th><td>diverse@inria.fr </td></tr>\n</table
 >\n<div>*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*</div><br><div style="font-family: arial\, helvet
 ica\, sans-serif\; font-size: 12pt\; color: #000000"><div style="font-family
 : arial\, helvetica\, sans-serif\; font-size: 12pt\; color: #000000"><div>Hi
  all\,&nbsp\;</div><div><br data-mce-bogus="1"></div><div>We're happy to hav
 e Gauthier Lyan&nbsp\;as our next DiverSE Coffee speaker. He'll be introduci
 ng a couple of frameworks for big data processing and use cases.</div><div><
 br data-mce-bogus="1"></div><div> In the Agenda:<br><br><div>- Apache NiFi f
 or Data flow integration (with a few examples and use cases)<br></div><div>-
  Apache Spark &amp\; its architecture (clustering\, scalability\, limitation
 s)</div><div>- How to use it locally (because it is a genius tool for data e
 ngineering\, even for small datasets)?</div><div>- How to simulate a cluster
  on a computer that has numerous cores and a lot of memory to bypass some lo
 cal limitations and enhance CPU intensive tasks performance?<br></div><div>-
  How to test you data engineering with a framework I made for my work?<br><b
 r>The presentation is held next Thursday\, somewhere in the dark side of the
  lab (Room Bréhat!) at 1 pm.<br><br>See you there!<br><br>Cheers\,</div></di
 v></div></div></body></html>
