BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:67d3ccfa-327c-4435-bf3a-641661085b73
SUMMARY:DiverSE Coffee: Dorian
DESCRIPTION:Hi all\, \n\nFor this week's presentation\, we're happy to have 
 Dorian Leroy presenting the current state of his work on the generalization 
 of model testing for DSLs.\n\nEnters Dorian:\n\n"Model-Driven Engineering (M
 DE) is a development paradigm that aims at coping with the complexity of sys
 tems by separating concerns through the use of models. \nA core characterist
 ic of MDE is the use of model transformations to analyze\, create or modify 
 models. Given their prominent role in MDE\, it is crucial to provide proper 
 means for testing the correctness of model transformations.\nWhile there is 
 a range of approaches for testing model transformations\, there are still ma
 ny open challenges as they are typically hardly configurable and tightly cou
 pled to a certain transformation language.\nIn this context\, we ground our 
 work in the fact that model transformation languages are a sort of domain-sp
 ecific languages (DSLs).\nThis allows us to investigate how to generalize mo
 del testing for any DSL and to use model transformations and the languages t
 hey conform to as a use case.\nIn this talk\, I will present the current sta
 te of our work and the upcoming steps."\n\nThe presentation is held in Room 
 Minquiers at 1 p.m.\n\nCheers\,
LOCATION:"Rennes-Salle Minquiers (B025)" <rennes-salle_minquiers@zimbra-loca
 l.inria.fr>
