BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:68f14615-bf12-46ce-87d4-f4b806bb1fa9
SUMMARY:DiverSE Coffee
DESCRIPTION:Hi all\, \n\nWe are happy to receive Maxime Bricet as a guest sp
 eaker for our next DiverSE Coffee . \nFor those who haven't meet Maxime alre
 ady\, he will be closely working with the team on a European Project called 
 " MyCarlot: Smart parking supported by predictive analytics to ease city tra
 ffic". \n\n\nEnters Maxime: \n"After graduating from ESIR\, the university e
 ngineering school\, in IoT stream\, I had the opportunity to join MyCarlot a
 t the end of my internship at Incube\, the Eit startup incubator. \nMyCarlot
  is a European project for smart parking lots involving Reply\, the DFKI (Ge
 rman Research Centre for Artificial Intelligence)\, INRIA and CRF (Centro Ri
 cerche Fiat). To optimise parking in the cities\, MyCarLot will provide an i
 ntegrated solution\, leveraging on different types of sensors and communicat
 ion (including vehicle to infrastructure)\, backend service with advanced fe
 atures to enable dynamic parking allocation\, free parking lots prediction a
 nd applications for parking guidance. Our experimentation will take place in
  Rennes or Saint-Malo (France) thanks to the Rennes-Saint Malo lab. It will 
 be conducted during the year 2018 on behalf of EIT Digital\, the leading Eur
 opean open-innovation and go-to-market organisation . " \n" \n\nThe presenta
 tion is held in Minquiers room\, this Thursday at 1 p.m. \n\nCheers\, \n"
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<html><body id='htmlmode'><h3>The following is 
 a new meeting request:</h3>\n\n<p>\n<table border='0'>\n<tr><th align=left>S
 ubject:</th><td>DiverSE Coffee </td></tr>\n<tr><th align=left>Organiser:</th
 ><td>"Amine Benelallam" &lt\;amine.benelallam@inria.fr&gt\; </td></tr>\n</ta
 ble>\n<p>\n<table border='0'>\n<tr><th align=left>Location:</th><td>"Rennes-
 Salle Minquiers (B025)" &lt\;rennes-salle_minquiers@zimbra-local.inria.fr&gt
 \; </td></tr>\n<tr><th align=left>Resources:</th><td>"Rennes-Salle Minquiers
  (B025)" &lt\;rennes-salle_minquiers@zimbra-local.inria.fr&gt\; (Lieu : Renn
 es\, Bâtiment : B\, Étage : bleu\, Salle : B025) </td></tr>\n<tr><th align=l
 eft>Time:</th><td>Thursday\, 25 January\, 2018\, 1:00:00 PM - 2:00:00 PM GMT
  +01:00 Brussels\, Copenhagen\, Madrid\, Paris\n </td></tr></table>\n<p>\n<t
 able border='0'>\n<tr><th align=left>Invitees:</th><td>diverse@inria.fr\; ma
 xime.bricet@irisa.fr </td></tr>\n</table>\n<div>*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*</div><br
 ><div style="font-family: times new roman\, new york\, times\, serif\; font-
 size: 12pt\; color: #000000"><div><div style="background-color: #ffffff\;" d
 ata-mce-style="background-color: #ffffff\;">Hi all\,&nbsp\;</div><div style=
 "background-color: #ffffff\;" data-mce-style="background-color: #ffffff\;"><
 br></div><div style="background-color: #ffffff\;" data-mce-style="background
 -color: #ffffff\;">We are happy to receive Maxime Bricet as a guest speaker 
 for our next&nbsp\;<span class="lG" style="background-color: rgba(251\, 246\
 , 167\, 0.5)\; outline: transparent dashed 1px\;" data-mce-style="background
 -color: rgba(251\, 246\, 167\, 0.5)\; outline: transparent dashed 1px\;">Div
 erSE</span>&nbsp\;<span class="lG" style="background-color: rgba(251\, 246\,
  167\, 0.5)\; outline: transparent dashed 1px\;" data-mce-style="background-
 color: rgba(251\, 246\, 167\, 0.5)\; outline: transparent dashed 1px\;">Coff
 ee</span>.</div><div style="background-color: #ffffff\;" data-mce-style="bac
 kground-color: #ffffff\;">For those who haven't&nbsp\;meet Maxime already\, 
 he will be closely working with the team on a European Project called "<stro
 ng><span style="background-color: #ffffff\;" data-mce-style="background-colo
 r: #ffffff\;">MyCarlot:&nbsp\;</span><span style="font-size: 12pt\; backgrou
 nd-color: #ffffff\;" data-mce-style="font-size: 12pt\; background-color: #ff
 ffff\;">Smart parking supported by predictive analytics to ease city traffic
 ".</span></strong></div><div style="background-color: #ffffff\;" data-mce-st
 yle="background-color: #ffffff\;"><strong><span style="font-size: 12pt\; bac
 kground-color: #ffffff\;" data-mce-style="font-size: 12pt\; background-color
 : #ffffff\;"><br></span></strong></div><div><br></div><div>Enters Maxime:</d
 iv><div><span style="background-color: #ffffff\;" data-mce-style="background
 -color: #ffffff\;">"After graduating from<span style="background-color: #fff
 fff\;" data-mce-style="background-color: #ffffff\;">&nbsp\;ESIR\, the univer
 sity&nbsp\;engineering&nbsp\;school\, in IoT stream\, I had the opportunity&
 nbsp\;to join MyCarlot at the end of my internship at Incube\, the Eit&nbsp\
 ;startup incubator.</span></span></div><div><span style="background-color: #
 ffffff\;" data-mce-style="background-color: #ffffff\;">MyCarlot is a Europea
 n project for smart parking lots involving Reply\, the DFKI (German Research
  Centre for Artificial Intelligence)\, INRIA and CRF (Centro Ricerche Fiat).
  To optimise parking in the cities\, MyCarLot will provide an integrated sol
 ution\, leveraging on different types of sensors and communication (includin
 g vehicle to infrastructure)\, backend service with advanced features to ena
 ble dynamic parking allocation\, free parking lots prediction and applicatio
 ns for parking guidance. Our experimentation will take place in Rennes or Sa
 int-Malo (France) thanks to the Rennes-Saint Malo lab. It will be conducted 
 during the year 2018 on behalf of EIT Digital\, the leading European open-in
 novation and go-to-market organisation.</span>"</div><div>"</div><div><br></
 div><div>The presentation is held in Minquiers room\, this Thursday at 1 p.m
