BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:695ef845-bc9f-4b51-8664-7593f68b68a1
SUMMARY:[SEMINAR] Minimum configurations in pairwise testing of feature mode
 ls (A. Hervieu)
DESCRIPTION:\nThe ever-growing diversity of users and requirements for softw
 are systems forces software industry to build more and more customizable sys
 tems. Feature models offer designers a compact way to represent the various 
 features in a product or a product family. The consequence of this increased
  variability for testers is that instead of verifying one system\, testers h
 ave to verify a large number of configurations or even a large number of com
 plete systems. Combinatorial interaction testing offers a promising solution
  to sample the set of configurations and focus testing on a subset of intera
 ctions that might lead to errors. This work investigates constraint programm
 ing to generate the minimum number of configurations that cover all pair-wis
 e interactions. \n
LOCATION:Lipari
