BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:77141c9b-bc06-4a49-8cb9-af0087dfb1aa
SUMMARY:[SEMINAR] Model-based (Mechatronic) Product Design (M. Kleiner)
DESCRIPTION:Designing a mechatronic product is the activity of creating a co
 mplete and consistent digital mockup of a complex system based on expertises
  from various scientific areas (functions\, components\, form features\, mul
 ti-physical behaviour\, etc.). It shares many similarities with the engineer
 ing of a software product. We will present some research work on applying so
 ftware engineering techniques\, in particular model-driven engineering (MDE)
  and constraint-based reasoning\, to the context of mechatronic products des
 ign. A theoretical and practical architecture is proposed\, in which the cor
 e idea is to use an (evolving) federation of (meta-)models\, transformations
  and projections as a collaborative data sharing and inference platform. Bas
 ed on different usecases\, we describe how MDE concepts can be successfully 
 adapted and allow to overcome some of the current issues (tools interoperabi
 lity\, formal verification\, support of innovative design processes\, etc.).
  We also raise a number of original challenges for which current MDE tools e
 ither lack capabilities or maturity and propose according research direction
 s. \n\nhttp://www.lsis.org/kleinerm/ 
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<html><body><h3>La réunion suivante a été modif
 iée :</h3>\n\n<p>\n<table border='0'>\n<tr><th align=left>Sujet :</th><td>[S
 EMINAR] Model-based (Mechatronic) Product Design (M. Kleiner) </td></tr>\n<t
 r><th align=left>Organisateur:</th><td>"Benoit Combemale" &lt\;benoit.combem
 ale@irisa.fr&gt\; </td></tr>\n</table>\n<p>\n<table border='0'>\n<tr><th ali
 gn=left>Endroit :</th><td>"Rennes-Salle Sicile (F302\, audioconférence)" &lt
 \;rennes-salle_sicile@zimbra-local.inria.fr&gt\; </td></tr>\n<tr><th align=l
 eft>Ressources :</th><td>"Rennes-Salle Sicile (F302\, audioconférence)" &lt\
 ;rennes-salle_sicile@zimbra-local.inria.fr&gt\; (Lieu : Rennes\, Bâtiment : 
 F\, Étage : vert\, Salle : F302) [MODIFIÉ]</td></tr>\n<tr><th align=left>Heu
 re:</th><td>Lundi 3 Juin 2013\, 16:30:00 - 17:30:00 GMT +01:00 Bruxelles\, C
 openhague\, Madrid\, Paris [MODIFIÉ]\n </td></tr></table>\n<p>\n<table borde
 r='0'>\n<tr><th align=left>Invités:</th><td>aleksandar.milenkosky@irisa.fr\;
  marinela.ciolfi-felice@inria.fr\; maxime.tricoire@irisa.fr\; yorick.perret@
 inria.fr\; guillaume.becan@inria.fr\; vincent.fontanella@inria.fr\; fabien.c
 oulon@inria.fr\; sana.ben-nasr@inria.fr\; francisco.acosta@inria.fr\; franci
 sco.moyano@irisa.fr\; sean.sedwards@inria.fr ... </td></tr>\n</table>\n<div>
 *~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*</div><br>Designing a mechatronic product is the activity
  of creating a complete and consistent digital mockup of a complex system ba
 sed on expertises from various scientific areas (functions\, components\, fo
 rm features\, multi-physical behaviour\, etc.). It shares many similarities 
 with the engineering of a software product. We will present some research wo
 rk on applying software engineering techniques\, in particular model-driven 
 engineering (MDE) and constraint-based reasoning\, to the context of mechatr
 onic products design. A theoretical and practical architecture is proposed\,
  in which the core idea is to use an (evolving) federation of (meta-)models\
 , transformations and projections as a collaborative data sharing and infere
 nce platform. Based on different usecases\, we describe how MDE concepts can
  be successfully adapted and allow to overcome some of the current issues (t
 ools interoperability\, formal verification\, support of innovative design p
 rocesses\, etc.). We also raise a number of original challenges for which cu
 rrent MDE tools either lack capabilities or maturity and propose according r
 esearch directions. <br><br>http://www.lsis.org/kleinerm/ </body></html>
LOCATION:"Rennes-Salle Sicile (F302\, audioconférence)" <rennes-salle_sicile
 @zimbra-local.inria.fr>
