BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:771923cb-1228-4d4b-9429-d6703e905c47
SUMMARY:[SEMINAR] Business Intelligence and Cloud-Computing (O. Ben David)
DESCRIPTION:\nGiven the importance of stored data by companies and their inc
 reasing needs in analysis. We can see many business intelligence solutions c
 oming out to address them. These solutions are mostly based on DBMS (data-ba
 se management system)\, system whose boundaries are beginning to be felt. \n
 The time for accessing resources become too long and some analysis are too c
 omplex to be performed by those DBMS. In this context new kind of database h
 ave been developed for the purpose to administer large amounts of data with 
 better performance. \nFurthermore\, distributed services are beginning to ta
 ke a new look with the emerging concept of cloud computing. Services can be 
 developed\, managed\, owned and used by multiple stakeholders on different d
 evices. \nIn this talk\, I will present in more details my internship work. 
 This internship was in an industrial context about business intelligence sol
 utions. Also I will briefly introduce cloud-computing\, NoSQL DBMS and busin
 ess intelligence concepts\, then I will present my proposal around the ETL (
 extract transform load) part of a BI solution and finally I will give the co
 nclusion of this work. \n
LOCATION:lipari
