BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:7d8920fe-ee10-46da-9bde-ea8c0338a95a
SUMMARY:DiverSE Coffee
DESCRIPTION:Hi all\, \n\nWe're happy to have Alexandre Rio as a speaker for 
 our next DiverSE Coffee.\n\nHe will be presenting his MODELS'18 paper entitl
 ed: "Efficient use of local energy: An activity oriented modeling to guide D
 emand Side Management"\n\nEnters Alexandre: \n"Self-consumption of renewable
  energies is defined as electricity that is produced from renewable energy s
 ources\, not injected to the distribution or transmission grid or instantane
 ously withdrawn from the grid and consumed by the owner of the power product
 ion unit or by associates directly contracted to the producer. Designing sol
 utions in favor of self-consumption for small industries or city districts i
 s challenging. It consists in designing an energy production system made of 
 solar panels\, wind turbines\, batteries that fit the annual weather predict
 ion and the industrial or human activity. In this context\, this paper repor
 ts the context of this business domain\, its challenges\, and the applicatio
 n of modeling that leads to a solution. Through this article\, we highlight 
 the essentials of a domain specific modeling language designed to let domain
  experts run their own simulations\, we compare with existing practices that
  exist in such a company and we discuss the benefits and the limits of the u
 se of modeling in such context."\n\nThe presentation is held in Room Sein on
  Thursday at 1 pm.\n\nRegards\,
ATTENDEE;CN=diverse;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=NEEDS-ACTION;RSVP=TRUE:mai
 lto:diverse@inria.fr
ATTENDEE;CN=Alexandre Rio;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=NEEDS-ACTION;RSVP=TR
 UE:mailto:alexandre.rio@irisa.fr
ORGANIZER;CN=Juliana Alves pereira:mailto:juliana.alves-pereira@irisa.fr
DTSTART;TZID="Europe/Brussels":20181115T130000
DTEND;TZID="Europe/Brussels":20181115T140000
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CLASS:PUBLIC
X-MICROSOFT-CDO-INTENDEDSTATUS:BUSY
TRANSP:OPAQUE
