BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:8463d19e-bda0-4f97-8bda-efe5797da13b
SUMMARY:DiverSE Coffee: Nicolas Harrand
DESCRIPTION:Greetings everyone\,\n\nIn this week's talk\, Nicolas Harrand is
  defying common sense software engineering.\n\nArmed with his strong belief 
 in diversification\, he explores source code transformations and their relat
 ions with test suites to show how NOT FRAGILE software is. \n\nEnters Nicola
 s: \n\n"There is a common assumption that software is fragile and that a sin
 gle change will often break it. On the contrary\, we believe that software i
 s plastic\, meaning that it can take multiple transformations (even changing
  its semantic) and still fulfill its original purpose. \nIn this talk\, I'll
  present our work on software diversification in which we explore source cod
 e transformations and their relations with test suites."\n\nThe presentation
  is held Thursday\, June 15th\, in Aurigny room at 1.p.m.\n\nSee you there!
LOCATION:"Rennes-Salle Aurigny (D165\, visioconférence)" <rennes-salle_aurig
 ny@zimbra-local.inria.fr>
ATTENDEE;CN=Nicolas Harrand;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=NEEDS-ACTION;RSVP=
 TRUE:mailto:nicolas.harrand@irisa.fr
