BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:8ccd0cbb-4fe6-4e9a-a8ae-612a02662651
SUMMARY:DiverSE coffee
DESCRIPTION:Hi All\, \n\nIn our DiverSE coffee of 21st November\, Ludovic wi
 ll make a rehearsal of his defense in front of all the team. \n\nEnters @Lud
 ovic: “Adaptive systems can be optimised at runtime due to errors. One can u
 se the model-driven engineering methodology to implement them. But\, gathere
 d information may not be known with high confidence. And effects of optimisa
 tions actions may suffer from a delay incompatible with rapid detection of e
 rrors. These come with a global challenge for software engineers: how to rep
 resent uncertain knowledge that can be efficiently queried and to represent 
 ongoing actions in order to improve adaptation processes? To tackle this cha
 llenge\, this thesis defends the need for a unified modelling framework whic
 h includes\, besides all traditional elements\, temporal and uncertainty as 
 first-class concepts. I will present two contributions towards this vision: 
 a temporal context model and a language for uncertain data." \n\nThe present
 ation is held in room Turing-Petri at 1 pm. \n\nKind regards\, \nJuliana. \n
 "
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<html><body id='htmlmode'><h3>The following mee
 ting has been forwarded:</h3>\n\n<p>\n<table border='0'>\n<tr><th align=left
 >Subject:</th><td>DiverSE Coffee [Ludovic Mouline] [MODIFIED]</td></tr>\n<tr
 ><th align=left>Organizer:</th><td>sophie.maupile@irisa.fr </td></tr>\n</tab
 le>\n<p>\n<table border='0'>\n<tr><th align=left>Location:</th><td>"Rennes-S
 alle Turing-Petri (G109-G107\, Vidéoprojecteur\, Salle séparable en deux) [R
 ]" &lt\;rennes-salle_turing-petri@zimbra-local.inria.fr&gt\; </td></tr>\n<tr
 ><th align=left>Resources:</th><td>"Rennes-Salle Turing-Petri (G109-G107\, V
 idéoprojecteur\, Salle séparable en deux) [R]" &lt\;rennes-salle_turing-petr
 i@zimbra-local.inria.fr&gt\; (Rennes-Salle Turing-Petri (G109-G107\, Vidéopr
 ojecteur\, Salle séparable en deux) [R]) </td></tr>\n<tr><th align=left>Time
 :</th><td>Thursday\, November 21\, 2019\, 1:00:00 PM - 2:00:00 PM GMT +01:00
  Brussels\, Copenhagen\, Madrid\, Paris\n </td></tr></table>\n<p>\n<table bo
 rder='0'>\n<tr><th align=left>Invitees:</th><td>juliana.alves-pereira@irisa.
 fr\; diverse@inria.fr\; nelly.bencomo@inria.fr\; ludovic.mouline@irisa.fr </
 td></tr>\n</table>\n<div>*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*</div><br><div style="font-famil
 y: arial\, helvetica\, sans-serif\; font-size: 11pt\; color: #000000"><div><
 div>Hi All\,&nbsp\;</div><div><br></div><div>In our DiverSE coffee of 21st N
 ovember\, Ludovic will make a rehearsal of his defense in front of all the t
 eam.</div><div><br></div><div>Enters @Ludovic: “Adaptive systems can be opti
 mised at runtime due to errors. One can use the model-driven engineering met
 hodology to implement them. But\, gathered information may not be known with
  high confidence. And effects of optimisations actions may suffer from a del
 ay incompatible with rapid detection of errors. These come with a global cha
 llenge for software engineers: how to represent uncertain knowledge that can
  be efficiently queried and to represent ongoing actions in order to improve
  adaptation processes? To tackle this challenge\, this thesis defends the ne
 ed for a unified modelling framework which includes\, besides all traditiona
 l elements\, temporal and uncertainty as first-class concepts. I will presen
 t two contributions towards this vision: a temporal context model and a lang
 uage for uncertain data."</div><div><br></div><div>The presentation is held 
 in room&nbsp\;Turing-Petri&nbsp\;at 1 pm.&nbsp\;</div><div><br></div><div>Ki
 nd regards\,</div><div>Juliana.</div></div><div style="font-family: arial\, 
 helvetica\, sans-serif\; font-size: 12pt\; color: #000000\;" data-mce-style=
 "font-family: arial\, helvetica\, sans-serif\; font-size: 12pt\; color: #000
 000\;"><div style="font-family: arial\, helvetica\, sans-serif\; font-size: 
 12pt\; color: #000000\;" data-mce-style="font-family: arial\, helvetica\, sa
 ns-serif\; font-size: 12pt\; color: #000000\;"></div></div></div></body></ht
 ml>"
