BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:90659324-455e-45a3-8385-5271bc95afc1
SUMMARY:Variability in Modeling Languages => PLDI'14
DESCRIPTION:Let's continue the work for managing the variability of language
  family in the Kermeta language workbench. \n\n@Suresh: would you start by p
 resenting the current status (syntactic variability in Kermeta\, and semanti
 c variability in Neverlang)? \n\nIdentified challenges for this new work: \n
 * semantic composition operator for Kermeta/OCL/Ecore-based language units (
 leveraging on our experience in Neverlang) \n* "multi-dimensional" variabili
 ty modeling (expressiveness\, semantic variation point\, implementation choi
 ces\, tooling) \n==> which actually is not multi-dimensional since the dimen
 sion are related! \n\nPossible case study: statechart \n\nPeople involved: S
 uresh\, Benoit\, Benoit\, Olivier\, Mathieu and Jean-Marc. \n\nTarget: PLDI\
 ; submission ~mid-november. 
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<html><body><h3>La réunion suivante a été modif
 iée :</h3>\n\n<p>\n<table border='0'>\n<tr><th align=left>Sujet :</th><td>Va
 riability in Modeling Languages =&gt\; PLDI'14 </td></tr>\n<tr><th align=lef
 t>Organisateur:</th><td>"Benoit Combemale" &lt\;benoit.combemale@irisa.fr&gt
 \; </td></tr>\n</table>\n<p>\n<table border='0'>\n<tr><th align=left>Endroit
  :</th><td>"Rennes-Salle Sicile (F302\, audioconférence)" &lt\;rennes-salle_
 sicile@zimbra-local.inria.fr&gt\; </td></tr>\n<tr><th align=left>Ressources 
 :</th><td>"Rennes-Salle Sicile (F302\, audioconférence)" &lt\;rennes-salle_s
 icile@zimbra-local.inria.fr&gt\; (Rennes-Salle Sicile (F302\, audioconférenc
 e)) </td></tr>\n<tr><th align=left>Heure:</th><td>Jeudi 27 Juin 2013\, 09:00
 :00 - 12:00:00 GMT +01:00 Bruxelles\, Copenhague\, Madrid\, Paris [MODIFIÉ]\
 n </td></tr></table>\n<p>\n<table border='0'>\n<tr><th align=left>Invités:</
 th><td>suresh.pillay@irisa.fr\; mathieu.acher@irisa.fr\; olivier.barais@iris
 a.fr\; benoit.baudry@inria.fr\; jean-marc.jezequel@irisa.fr </td></tr>\n</ta
 ble>\n<div>*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*</div><br>Let's continue the work for managing
  the variability of language family in the Kermeta language workbench. <br><
 br>@Suresh: would you start by presenting the current status (syntactic vari
 ability in Kermeta\, and semantic variability in Neverlang)? <br><br>Identif
 ied challenges for this new work: <br>* semantic composition operator for Ke
 rmeta/OCL/Ecore-based language units (leveraging on our experience in Neverl
 ang) <br>* "multi-dimensional" variability modeling (expressiveness\, semant
 ic variation point\, implementation choices\, tooling) <br>==&gt\; which act
 ually is not multi-dimensional since the dimension are related! <br><br>Poss
 ible case study: statechart <br><br>People involved: Suresh\, Benoit\, Benoi
 t\, Olivier\, Mathieu and Jean-Marc. <br><br>Target: PLDI\; submission ~mid-
 november. </body></html>
LOCATION:"Rennes-Salle Sicile (F302\, audioconférence)" <rennes-salle_sicile
 @zimbra-local.inria.fr>
ATTENDEE;CN=Suresh Pillay;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=NEEDS-ACTION;RSVP=TR
 UE:mailto:suresh.pillay@irisa.fr
ATTENDEE;CN=Mathieu Acher;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=DECLINED:mailto:math
 ieu.acher@irisa.fr
ATTENDEE;CN=Olivier Barais;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=ACCEPTED:mailto:oli
