BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:921d621f-9bb7-4797-b8fe-785ea21003f8
SUMMARY:[SEMINAR] Semantic Enrichment of Software Product Lines (Bosco)
DESCRIPTION:Software Product Lines (SPLs) have evolved and gained attention 
 as one of the most promising approaches for software reuse. Feature models a
 re the main technique to represent domain variability in SPLs. However\, the
 re are other domain aspects\, besides variability\, which cannot be expresse
 d in a feature model. Moreover\, these models were not designed to facilitat
 e information retrieval\, interoperability and inference. In contrast\, onto
 logies seem to be the best solution\, because they meet these requirements. 
 Therefore\, this work presents an approach for semantic enrichment in SPLs b
 ased on ontologies. Our proposal provides methods to add domain information 
 besides variability description\, and a top-ontology that specifies generic 
 concepts and relations in a SPL. The proposed approach reuses the existing S
 PL feature model\, adding semantic descriptions in a less intrusive way than
  modifying the feature model notation. A case study is presented to evaluate
  the benefits of adopting the approach. \n
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<html><body><h3>Nouvelle demande de réunion ci-
 dessous :</h3>\n\n<p>\n<table border='0'>\n<tr><th align=left>Sujet :</th><t
 d>[SEMINAR] Semantic Enrichment of Software Product Lines (Bosco) </td></tr>
 \n<tr><th align=left>Organisateur:</th><td>"Benoit Combemale" &lt\;benoit.co
 mbemale@irisa.fr&gt\; </td></tr>\n</table>\n<p>\n<table border='0'>\n<tr><th
  align=left>Endroit :</th><td>Rennes-Salle Lipari (F202) </td></tr>\n<tr><th
  align=left>Ressources :</th><td>Rennes-Salle Lipari (F202) (Lieu : Rennes\,
  Bâtiment : F\, Étage : orange\, Salle : F202) </td></tr>\n<tr><th align=lef
 t>Heure:</th><td>Jeudi 19 Avril 2012\, 13:30:00 - 14:30:00 GMT +01:00 Bruxel
 les\, Copenhague\, Madrid\, Paris\n </td></tr></table>\n<p>\n<table border='
 0'>\n<tr><th align=left>Invités:</th><td>"erwan" &lt\;erwan.bousse@gmail.com
 &gt\;\; "Antonio-Junior Mattos" &lt\;antonio-junior.mattos@irisa.fr&gt\;\; "
 An Phung-Khac" &lt\;an.phungkhac@inria.fr&gt\;\; "Julien Richard-Foy" &lt\;j
 ulien.richard-foy@irisa.fr&gt\;\; "Joao Ferreira_filho" &lt\;joao.ferreira_f
 ilho@inria.fr&gt\;\; "Suresh Pillay" &lt\;suresh.pillay@irisa.fr&gt\;\; "Jea
 n-Emile Dartois" &lt\;jean-emile.dartois@inria.fr&gt\;\; "Jonathan Marchand"
  &lt\;jonathan.yves.marchand@irisa.fr&gt\;\; "Hanen Haouas" &lt\;hanen.haoua
 s@inria.fr&gt\;\; "Xavier Dolques" &lt\;xavier.dolques@inria.fr&gt\;\;  ... 
 </td></tr>\n</table>\n<div>*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*</div><br><div style='font-fam
 ily:times new roman\,new york\,times\,serif\; font-size: 12pt\; color: #0000
 00\;'>Software Product Lines (SPLs) have evolved and gained attention as one
  of the most promising approaches for software reuse. Feature models are the
  main technique to represent domain variability in SPLs. However\, there are
  other domain aspects\, besides variability\, which cannot be expressed in a
  feature model. Moreover\, these models were not designed to facilitate info
 rmation retrieval\, interoperability and inference. In contrast\, ontologies
  seem to be the best solution\, because they meet these requirements. Theref
 ore\, this work presents an approach for semantic enrichment in SPLs based o
 n ontologies. Our proposal provides methods to add domain information beside
 s variability description\, and a top-ontology that specifies generic concep
 ts and relations in a SPL. The proposed approach reuses the existing SPL fea
 ture model\, adding semantic descriptions in a less intrusive way than modif
 ying the feature model notation. A case study is presented to evaluate the b
 enefits of adopting the approach.<br></div></body></html>
LOCATION:Rennes-Salle Lipari (F202)
