BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:a0e0394c-f4a8-4040-935e-26121842abb4
SUMMARY:DiverSE Coffee:  Nguepi Armando
DESCRIPTION:Hi all\, \n\nThe story "Testing Configurable Software" continues
  with a presentation staring Nguepi Armando. \n\nArmando is pursuing his Mas
 ter's degree in Software Engineering at the University of Namur in Belgium. 
 \nHe is spending his last semester interning in the DiverSE team\, under the
  supervision of Mathieu Archer\, for the period of October 1st until January
  31st. \nThe topic of his internship orbits around testing configurable soft
 ware. \n\nEnters Armando: \n"How to test configurable software? \nIn this pr
 esentation\, we describe an approach using variability techniques to test co
 nfigurable software. We apply this approach to a web-application generator\,
  JHipster. \nThe first part of the presentation describes configurable softw
 are exemplified by JHipster while illustrating why it is a good candidate. \
 nThe second part presents previous work and results. The last part of presen
 tation describes our work that consists to replicate previous work on anothe
 r version of JHipster and evaluate and report the efforts to update tests in
 frastructure built in previous work\, according to the evolution of JHipster
 . We also want to give information to help automatize JHipster testing." \n\
 nThe presentation is held Thursday 7th in room Minquiers at 1 p.m. \n\nCheer
 s\, 
LOCATION:"Rennes-Salle Minquiers (B025)" <rennes-salle_minquiers@zimbra-loca
 l.inria.fr>
ATTENDEE;CN=Amine Benelallam;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=NEEDS-ACTION;RSVP
 =TRUE:mailto:amine.benelallam@inria.fr
