BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:a9b67009-9fd0-4a4e-8e59-c7644f0e9f8c
SUMMARY:Interview Marcellino
DESCRIPTION:Numéro de Téléphone de Marcelino : (+53) 53 22 22 06\n\nE-mail :
  \nDear Professor Bourcier:\n\nFrom a former colleague and personal friend c
 urrently studying his Ph.D. at INRIA\, Inti Gonzales\,  I learned about poss
 ible openings as research engineer at Diverse group.  I'm writing you to exp
 ress my desire to work in your team and help to the best of my capacities to
  achieve their goals. I believe that may qualifications and previous work ex
 perience will allow me to perform positively as research engineer at Diverse
 .\n\n \n\nI first had the opportunity to create a large framework with WatDi
 s(http://www.water-simulation.com/wsp/2012/11/19/watdis-the-little-challenge
 r/)\, a system for the analysis of water pressure distributions networks. Wa
 tDis was constructed in a way that allowed the system grow smoothly and with
 out substantial changes in the philosophy of development. A plug-in system w
 as developed inspired in Equinox. The components were decoupled and interact
 ed by means of a message manager. Messages should be asynchronous when possi
 ble to allow the message system to batch them.  Visual representation of the
  model was decoupled from the model itself in order augment reusability\n\n 
 \n\nLater\, I had the opportunity to participate in another ambitious projec
 t: DiPPo\, CIMNE's platform for image processing. CIMNE has a clear idea on 
 what they want: to create many specific purposes tools using the same code b
 ase. Since the image processing and visualization libraries (ITK and VTK) we
 re given as requirements\, we give ourselves to the task of reusing controll
 er code.  We were able to do this by creating a framework and a methodology.
  Students were called on to work on some experimental tools to see how the c
 oncepts in DiPPo behave and they were able to rapidly create image processin
 g tools reusing one each other's controllers. From my experiences in DiPPo\,
  I think it would be most interesting for me to work on MDD applied to the f
 ield of specific purpose imaging applications.\n\n \n\nI hold a Master in Di
 gital Signal Processing (2013)  and a Bachelor in Computer Science since 200
 8. I have been programming since I was 15 and 15 years later still feels fun
  and rewarding.\n\n \n\nSoftware engineering has been one of my interest and
  likes since early days of university in which I ambitioned to create large 
 software systems. I soon realized that my programming skills back then got m
 e stuck  with bugs and strong coupling at an early stage of the development 
 process. I began my personal search and I have read every software engineeri
 ng material I could put my hands on.\n\n \n\nInti was kind enough in letting
  me know about the DIVERSIFY project. I found the ideas there quite advanced
  and extremely interesting. It would be an honor and a pleasure to be involv
 ed in such cutting edge investigations and progresses in software developmen
 t. I worked on an  implemented a version of the fast messy genetic algorithm
  for Transparent Blue. I'm aware of evolutive computing concepts and I belie
 ve I could be very helpful in DIVERSIFY.\n\n \n\nFinally if you have the tim
 e\, please take a look at: https://www.dropbox.com/s/m67jm9mi23kpmyh/MyOptim
 izer.rar.  Is an small prototype I created to show you. The project contains
  the plug-in  system I developed for WatDis in C# (released to open source b
 y Transparent Blue) . There I show an small platform for the optimization of
  functions using genetic algorithms. The systems automatically creates GUI f
 or these functions extracting parameters by means of code discovering using 
 reflection.\n\n \n\n \n\nI would like to express again my desire to work wit
 h your team. I believe that INRIA is one of the leading voices in software e
 ngineering in the world and it would be wonderful to be part of it.\n\n \n\n
 Best regards\n\nMarcelino Rodríguez\n\n \n\nP.S. In order to keep the motiva
 tion letter concise and brief\, I let out some comments I first included. Th
 ey  are some thoughts\, opinions and how I feel about some issues. I give th
 em as P.S. just in case you may have an spare time.\n\n \n\n1. In WatDis\, t
 he work of Inti Gonzales was essential\, he created the Transparent Blue hyd
 raulic engine and worked on most of the features. He also work very hard in 
 the calibration of the network using my fmGA implementation.\n\n \n\n2. The 
 beauty of software of engineering is that is an act of creation. There is no
 w way to know forehand is your ideas are going to make the system grow smoot
 hly\, bug-free and fail safe. It's like music\, you don't know if this is go
 od: you feel it.\n\nPerhaps you'll like to listen to my music at https://sou
 ndcloud.com/elgatoqueandasolo.\n\n \n\n3. In our first meetings with the hyd
 raulic engineers for the WatDis project\, they talk about many things. They 
 talk of water distribution networks\, GiS compatibility\, automatic demand a
 ssignment\, calibration by means of Genetic Algorithms\, multiple calculatio
 n engines... I did know nothing of hydraulic back then (still don't) and I t
 ried to dissimulate my surprise when I learned  (in that meeting)  that the 
 water tank has to be higher than the pile in order for the water to flow to 
 your hands.\n\n \n\nAnyhow\, my point is that I realized that I had to creat
 e a system that will permit the smooth development of features I could even 
 imagine in the moment. I would be like a soup\, absorbing all ingredients a 
 chief would want to put in it.  You want chicken in the soup? Ok. Potatoes? 
 no problem. Noodles? OK.  So...you want to draw a network. OK. Now\, we must
  calculate it according to some method\, that's fine. Genetic Algorithms? Br
 ing it on. I like to cook and I like how WatDis turns on.\n\n \n\n4. I had t
 he opportunity to reuse many patterns from WatDis in DiPPo. This allow the r
 apid creation of many imaging software rapidly like BrainApp and Medula. Aor
 ta 4D Flow was refactored to use DiPPo in a matters of weeks.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<html><body><h3>Nouvelle demande de réunion ci-
 dessous :</h3>\n\n<p>\n<table border='0'>\n<tr><th align=left>Sujet :</th><t
