 tunity to participate in another ambitious project: DiPPo\, CIMNE's platform
  for image processing. CIMNE has a clear idea on what they want: to create m
 any specific purposes tools using the same code base. Since the image proces
 sing and visualization libraries (ITK and VTK) were given as requirements\, 
 we give ourselves to the task of reusing controller code.  We were able to d
 o this by creating a framework and a methodology. Students were called on to
  work on some experimental tools to see how the concepts in DiPPo behave and
  they were able to rapidly create image processing tools reusing one each ot
 her's controllers. From my experiences in DiPPo\, I think it would be most i
 nteresting for me to work on MDD applied to the field of specific purpose im
 aging applications.<br><br>&nbsp\;<br><br>I hold a Master in Digital Signal 
 Processing (2013)  and a Bachelor in Computer Science since 2008. I have bee
 n programming since I was 15 and 15 years later still feels fun and rewardin
 g.<br><br>&nbsp\;<br><br>Software engineering has been one of my interest an
 d likes since early days of university in which I ambitioned to create large
  software systems. I soon realized that my programming skills back then got 
 me stuck  with bugs and strong coupling at an early stage of the development
  process. I began my personal search and I have read every software engineer
 ing material I could put my hands on.<br><br>&nbsp\;<br><br>Inti was kind en
 ough in letting me know about the DIVERSIFY project. I found the ideas there
  quite advanced and extremely interesting. It would be an honor and a pleasu
 re to be involved in such cutting edge investigations and progresses in soft
 ware development. I worked on an  implemented a version of the fast messy ge
 netic algorithm for Transparent Blue. I'm aware of evolutive computing conce
 pts and I believe I could be very helpful in DIVERSIFY.<br><br>&nbsp\;<br><b
 r>Finally if you have the time\, please take a look at: https://www.dropbox.
 com/s/m67jm9mi23kpmyh/MyOptimizer.rar.  Is an small prototype I created to s
 how you. The project contains the plug-in  system I developed for WatDis in 
 C# (released to open source by Transparent Blue) . There I show an small pla
 tform for the optimization of functions using genetic algorithms. The system
 s automatically creates GUI for these functions extracting parameters by mea
 ns of code discovering using reflection.<br><br>&nbsp\;<br><br>&nbsp\;<br><b
 r>I would like to express again my desire to work with your team. I believe 
 that INRIA is one of the leading voices in software engineering in the world
  and it would be wonderful to be part of it.<br><br>&nbsp\;<br><br>Best rega
 rds<br><br>Marcelino Rodríguez<br><br>&nbsp\;<br><br>P.S. In order to keep t
 he motivation letter concise and brief\, I let out some comments I first inc
 luded. They  are some thoughts\, opinions and how I feel about some issues. 
 I give them as P.S. just in case you may have an spare time.<br><br>&nbsp\;<
 br><br>1. In WatDis\, the work of Inti Gonzales was essential\, he created t
 he Transparent Blue hydraulic engine and worked on most of the features. He 
 also work very hard in the calibration of the network using my fmGA implemen
 tation.<br><br>&nbsp\;<br><br>2. The beauty of software of engineering is th
 at is an act of creation. There is now way to know forehand is your ideas ar
 e going to make the system grow smoothly\, bug-free and fail safe. It's like
  music\, you don't know if this is good: you feel it.<br><br>Perhaps you'll 
 like to listen to my music at https://soundcloud.com/elgatoqueandasolo.<br><
 br>&nbsp\;<br><br>3. In our first meetings with the hydraulic engineers for 
 the WatDis project\, they talk about many things. They talk of water distrib
 ution networks\, GiS compatibility\, automatic demand assignment\, calibrati
