BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aa2bc53e-30ad-4512-a881-c621b53971ad
SUMMARY:DiverSE Coffee [Fabien Coulon]: "Shape-Diverse DSLs: Languages witho
 ut Borders (Vision Paper)"
DESCRIPTION:Hi all\, \n\nAs far as we can be from a world\, an economy and a
  democracy without borders\, let us enjoy for now language engineering witho
 ut borders starring Fabien Coulon.\nIn his talk\, he will be bringing us one
  step closer towards the language engineering utopia\, accepted at SLE'19.\n
 \nEnters Fabien: \n\n" Domain-Specific Languages (DSLs) manifest themselves 
 in remarkably diverse shapes\, ranging from internal DSLs embedded as a mere
  fluent API within a programming language\, to external DSLs with dedicated 
 syntax and tool support. Although different shapes have different pros and c
 ons\, combining them for a single language is problematic: language designer
 s usually commit to a particular shape early in the design process\, and it 
 is hard to reconsider this choice later. In this new ideas paper\, we envisi
 on a language engineering approach enabling (i) language users to manipulate
  language constructs in the most appropriate shape according to the task at 
 hand\, and (ii) language designers to combine the strengths of different tec
 hnologies for a single DSL. We report on early experiments and lessons learn
 ed building Prism\, our prototype approach to this problem. We illustrate it
 s applicability in the engineering of a simple shape-diverse DSL implemented
  conjointly in Rascal\, EMF\, and Java. We hope that our initial contributio
 n will raise the awareness of the community and encourage future research. "
 \n\nThe presentation is held in Minquiers at 1 pm.\n\nRegards\, \n
LOCATION:"Rennes-Salle Minquiers (B025\, Vidéoprojecteur )" <rennes-salle_mi
 nquiers@zimbra-local.inria.fr>
ATTENDEE;CN=Fabien Coulon;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=NEEDS-ACTION;RSVP=TR
 UE:mailto:fabien.coulon@inria.fr
ATTENDEE;CN=diverse;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=NEEDS-ACTION;RSVP=TRUE:mai
 lto:diverse@inria.fr
ATTENDEE;CN="Rennes-Salle Minquiers (B025, Vidéoprojecteur )";CUTYPE=RESOURC
 E;ROLE=NON-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=ACCEPTED:mailto:rennes-salle_minquiers@zimbr
 a-local.inria.fr
ORGANIZER;CN=Amine Benelallam:mailto:amine.benelallam@inria.fr
DTSTART;TZID="Europe/Brussels":20181025T130000
DTEND;TZID="Europe/Brussels":20181025T140000
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CLASS:PUBLIC
