BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ae5dcff0-eb96-4818-8c63-2121bed77e51
SUMMARY:Meeting on Language Engineering
DESCRIPTION:Let's welcome David\, who is a new PhD student in the team who w
 ill work on variability management in modeling languages.\nHe will be mainly
  involved in the collaboration with Thales as well as in the GEMOC project (
 and somehow in the Relate project). \n\nIt would be great to give him an ide
 a of our current activities in language engineering. \nHere is a tentative a
 genda for the meeting:\n- David: his background and experiences\n- Benoit: t
 he GEMOC project and the VaryMDE project\n- Olivier: Merge project\n- Didier
 : Kermeta: objectives\, tooling and current state (I can send you my slides 
 on this)\n- Benoit: introduction to model typing and variability management 
 in modeling languages\n- Erwan: Model cloning\, trace management and model V
 &V\n- Thomas: model typing\, metamodel extension...\n\nIt would be great to 
 plan for a presentation of 5/10minutes\, followed by questions. \n\nWe will 
 also try to plan for a triskell coffee in order to let David introduce his b
 ackground to the entire team.\n\nThanks\,\nBenoit
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<html><body><h3>Nouvelle demande de réunion ci-
 dessous :</h3>\n\n<p>\n<table border='0'>\n<tr><th align=left>Sujet :</th><t
 d>Meeting on Language Engineering </td></tr>\n<tr><th align=left>Organisateu
 r:</th><td>"Benoit Combemale" &lt\;benoit.combemale@irisa.fr&gt\; </td></tr>
 \n</table>\n<p>\n<table border='0'>\n<tr><th align=left>Endroit :</th><td>"R
 ennes-Salle Houat (C217)" &lt\;rennes-salle_houat@zimbra-local.inria.fr&gt\;
  </td></tr>\n<tr><th align=left>Ressources :</th><td>"Rennes-Salle Houat (C2
 17)" &lt\;rennes-salle_houat@zimbra-local.inria.fr&gt\; (Lieu : Rennes\, Bât
 iment : C\, Étage : orange\, Salle : C217) </td></tr>\n<tr><th align=left>He
 ure:</th><td>Lundi 2 Décembre 2013\, 14:00:00 - 17:00:00 GMT +01:00 Bruxelle
 s\, Copenhague\, Madrid\, Paris\n </td></tr></table>\n<p>\n<table border='0'
 >\n<tr><th align=left>Invités:</th><td>olivier.barais@irisa.fr\; didier.vojt
 isek@inria.fr\; thomas.degueule@inria.fr\; erwan.bousse@irisa.fr\; benoit.ba
 udry@inria.fr </td></tr>\n</table>\n<div>*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*</div><br>Let's 
 welcome David\, who is a new PhD student in the team who will work on variab
 ility management in modeling languages.<br>He will be mainly involved in the
  collaboration with Thales as well as in the GEMOC project (and somehow in t
 he Relate project). <br><br>It would be great to give him an idea of our cur
 rent activities in language engineering. <br>Here is a tentative agenda for 
 the meeting:<br>- David: his background and experiences<br>- Benoit: the GEM
 OC project and the VaryMDE project<br>- Olivier: Merge project<br>- Didier: 
 Kermeta: objectives\, tooling and current state (I can send you my slides on
  this)<br>- Benoit: introduction to model typing and variability management 
 in modeling languages<br>- Erwan: Model cloning\, trace management and model
  V&amp\;V<br>- Thomas: model typing\, metamodel extension...<br><br>It would
  be great to plan for a presentation of 5/10minutes\, followed by questions.
  <br><br>We will also try to plan for a triskell coffee in order to let Davi
 d introduce his background to the entire team.<br><br>Thanks\,<br>Benoit</bo
 dy></html>
LOCATION:"Rennes-Salle Houat (C217)" <rennes-salle_houat@zimbra-local.inria.
 fr>
