BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aea14d7c-6f8f-4f30-9671-a02eb403d2ff
SUMMARY:DiverSe Coffee
DESCRIPTION:Hello !! \n\nAfter last week's handover\, I would be in charge o
 f the DiverSE Coffee \;) \n\nThis DiverSE Coffee will be particular\, the Tu
 ring-Petri room being already booked we will do a hybrid coffee. \nSome of y
 ou can go to room Markov (the limit is 14) and for the others\, the presenta
 tion will be broadcasted at the same time (More information soon). \n\nDurin
 g today's coffee\, Corentin will present his work on VaryLaTeX done during h
 is internship. \n\nAbstract : VaryLaTeX is a tool that extracts variability 
 from standard LaTeX documents. The variability can be specified by the user 
 while writing a document or be generated automatically. We will see how it w
 orks with various examples of documents and how we can use VaryLaTeX to cust
 omize their output without having to touch the LaTeX source. We will also se
 e how we could use the tool to predict if a document is going to fit in a li
 mited amount of pages\, which can be useful when trying to tweak a paper to 
 respect a page limit. \n\nBest\, \nGwendal \n
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<html><body id='htmlmode'><h3>La réunion suivan
 te a été transférée :</h3>\n\n<p>\n<table border='0'>\n<tr><th align=left>Su
 jet :</th><td>Tr: DiverSe Coffee </td></tr>\n<tr><th align=left>Organisateur
 :</th><td>sophie.maupile@irisa.fr </td></tr>\n</table>\n<p>\n<table border='
 0'>\n<tr><th align=left>Endroit :</th><td>"Rennes-Salle Markov (G105\, Vidéo
 projecteur) [R]" &lt\;rennes-salle_markov@zimbra-local.inria.fr&gt\; </td></
 tr>\n<tr><th align=left>Ressources :</th><td>"Rennes-Salle Markov (G105\, Vi
 déoprojecteur) [R]" &lt\;rennes-salle_markov@zimbra-local.inria.fr&gt\; (Ren
 nes-Salle Markov (G105\, Vidéoprojecteur) [R]) </td></tr>\n<tr><th align=lef
 t>Heure:</th><td>Jeudi 10 Septembre 2020\, 13:00:00 - 14:00:00 GMT +01:00 Br
 uxelles\, Copenhague\, Madrid\, Paris\n </td></tr></table>\n<p>\n<table bord
 er='0'>\n<tr><th align=left>Invités:</th><td>gwendal.jouneaux@irisa.fr\; div
 erse@inria.fr </td></tr>\n</table>\n<div>*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*</div><br><div s
 tyle="font-family: arial\, helvetica\, sans-serif\; font-size: 12pt\; color:
  #000000"><div>Hello !!</div><div><br>After last week's handover\, I would b
 e in charge of the DiverSE Coffee \;)<br><br>This\n DiverSE Coffee will be p
 articular\, the Turing-Petri room being already booked we will do a hybrid c
 offee. </div><div>Some of you can go to room Markov (the limit is 14) and fo
 r the others\, the presentation will be broadcasted at the same time (More i
 nformation soon).</div><div><br>During today's coffee\, Corentin will presen
 t his work on VaryLaTeX done during his internship.</div><div><br></div><div
 >Abstract\n : VaryLaTeX is a tool that extracts variability from standard La
 TeX \ndocuments. The variability can be specified by the user while writing 
 a \ndocument or be generated automatically. We will see how it works with va
 rious examples of documents and how we can use VaryLaTeX to customize their 
 output without having to touch the LaTeX source. We will also see how we cou
 ld use the tool to predict if a document is going to fit in a \nlimited amou
 nt of pages\, which can be useful when trying to tweak a \npaper to respect 
 a page limit.<br><br>Best\,<br>Gwendal</div></div></body></html>
LOCATION:"Rennes-Salle Markov (G105\, Vidéoprojecteur) [R]" <rennes-salle_ma
 rkov@zimbra-local.inria.fr>
