BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:af0307e5-7ceb-4a0a-a619-a14fd5ca1b3c
SUMMARY:DiverSE Coffee
DESCRIPTION:Hi all\, \n\nA place to diversification. In this week's DiverSE 
 coffee\, Mathieu Acher will be presenting his LaText/latest on variability i
 n latex documents entitled "Vary\\LaTeX: Learning Paper Variants That Meet C
 onstraints".\nGiven a set of constraints (e.g. formatting instructions and p
 age limits)\, the proposed solution suggests a set of possible solutions ami
 d which the user has to choose a final either randomly or according to his c
 onsiderations.\n\n\nEnters Mathieu:\n\n" How to submit a research paper\, a 
 technical report\, a grant proposal\, or a curriculum vitae that respect imp
 osed constraints such as formatting instructions and page limits? It is a ch
 allenging task\, especially when coping with time pressure.  In this work\, 
 we present Vary\\LaTeX\, a solution based on variability\, constraint progra
 mming\, and machine learning techniques for documents written in LaTeX to me
 et constraints and deliver on time. \nUsers simply have to annotate LaTeX so
 urce files with variability information\, e.g.\, (de)activating portions of 
 text\, tuning figures' sizes\, or tweaking line spacing. Then\, a fully auto
 mated procedure learns constraints among boolean and numerical values for av
 oiding non-acceptable paper variants\,  and finally\, users can further conf
 igure their papers (e.g.\, aesthetic considerations) or pick a (random) pape
 r variant that meets constraints\, e.g.\, page limits. We describe our imple
 mentation and report the results of two experiences with Vary\\LaTeX." \n\nT
 he presentation will be held\, this Thursday\, at 1. p.m.\, in Room "TBA".\n
 \nkind regards\,\n
ATTENDEE;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=NEEDS-ACTION;RSVP=TRUE:mailto:diverse
 @inria.fr
ORGANIZER;CN=Amine Benelallam:mailto:amine.benelallam@inria.fr
