BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:b2f62763-f5f3-4b3f-82cc-bbffa4347de3
SUMMARY:DiverSE Coffee
DESCRIPTION:Hi all\, \n\nWe're happy to have Manuel tomorrow as our next Div
 erSE Coffee speaker. He will talk about JVM performance.\n\nEnters @Manuel: 
 In the last few years we went from a really limited choice of mainstream JVM
 s (Oracle’s JVM and Openjdk)\, to four wildly distributed JVM\, with the int
 roduction of OpenJ9\, recently open-sourced under Eclipse’s banner and Graal
 VM\, by Oracle Lab.\n\nAnd with such diversity arrive the question of the cr
 iteria on which to base our JVM choice.\n\nIn front of the limitless combina
 tion of criteria to base our choice on\, we will focus on the execution time
  of programs executed using Domain-Specific Languages (DSLs) developed in Ja
 va.\n\nWe are going to identify the force and weakness of multiple JVM by me
 asuring the execution time of multiple programs implemented on various DSLs 
 (described below). First\, we will compare their performance in term of pure
  execution time\, and in term of stability (does the performance of a single
  program vary between two executions?). Finally\, we will question the influ
 ence of the languages implementation patterns on DSLs performance.\n\nThe pr
 esentation is held this Thursday\, April 18th in room Minquiers at 1 pm. See
  you there!\n\nKind regards\,\nJuliana.
LOCATION:"Rennes-Salle Minquiers (B025\, Vidéoprojecteur )" <rennes-salle_mi
 nquiers@zimbra-local.inria.fr>
ATTENDEE;CN=juliana alves-pereira;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=NEEDS-ACTION
 ;RSVP=TRUE:mailto:juliana.alves-pereira@irisa.fr
