BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:bb78eda3-5bd3-45cd-b241-34c0f2c6c017
SUMMARY:DiverSE Coffee [Oscar] : On the relevance of pseudo tested methods
DESCRIPTION:Hi all\, \n\nFor our next diverSE coffee\, we're happy to have\,
  once again\, Oscar Luis Vera Pérez among us. \nHe will be presenting his la
 test results on investigating the relevance of pseudo tested methods on real
  open-source projects. \n\nEnters Oscar: \n"Pseudo-tested methods are those 
 whose code can be removed and the test suite is not able to detect the trans
 formation. \nIn this presentation\, we introduce an extension of the concept
  and explore the presence of such methods in real open source projects. \nWe
  also explore if they are relevant enough for developers to improve their te
 st suite." \n\nThe presentation is held this Thursday in room Minquiers at 1
  p.m. \n\nCheers\, \n
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<html><body id='htmlmode'><h3>The following is 
 a new meeting request:</h3>\n\n<p>\n<table border='0'>\n<tr><th align=left>S
 ubject:</th><td>DiverSE Coffee [Oscar] : On the relevance of pseudo tested m
 ethods </td></tr>\n<tr><th align=left>Organiser:</th><td>"Amine Benelallam" 
 &lt\;amine.benelallam@inria.fr&gt\; </td></tr>\n</table>\n<p>\n<table border
 ='0'>\n<tr><th align=left>Location:</th><td>"Rennes-Salle Minquiers (B025\, 
 Vidéoprojecteur )" &lt\;rennes-salle_minquiers@zimbra-local.inria.fr&gt\; </
 td></tr>\n<tr><th align=left>Resources:</th><td>"Rennes-Salle Minquiers (B02
 5\, Vidéoprojecteur )" &lt\;rennes-salle_minquiers@zimbra-local.inria.fr&gt\
 ; (Lieu : Rennes\, Bâtiment : B\, Étage : bleu\, Salle : B025) </td></tr>\n<
 tr><th align=left>Time:</th><td>Thursday\, 26 April\, 2018\, 13:00:00 - 14:0
 0:00 GMT +01:00 Brussels\, Copenhagen\, Madrid\, Paris\n </td></tr></table>\
 n<p>\n<table border='0'>\n<tr><th align=left>Invitees:</th><td>diverse@inria
 .fr </td></tr>\n</table>\n<div>*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*</div><br><div style="font
 -family: arial\, helvetica\, sans-serif\; font-size: 12pt\; color: #000000">
 <div>Hi all\,&nbsp\;</div><div><br data-mce-bogus="1"></div><div>For our nex
 t diverSE coffee\, we're happy&nbsp\;to have\, once again\, Oscar Luis Vera 
 Pérez among us.</div><div>He will be presenting his latest results on invest
 igating the relevance of pseudo tested methods on real open-source projects.
 </div><div><br data-mce-bogus="1"></div><div>Enters Oscar:</div><div>"Pseudo
 -tested methods are those whose code can be removed and the test suite is no
 t able to detect the transformation.<br></div><div>In this presentation\, we
  introduce an extension of the concept and explore the presence of such meth
 ods in real open source projects.</div><div>We also explore if they are rele
 vant enough for developers to improve their test suite."<br data-mce-bogus="
 1"></div><div><br data-mce-bogus="1"></div><div>The presentation is held thi
 s Thursday in room Minquiers at 1 p.m.</div><div><br data-mce-bogus="1"></di
 v><div>Cheers\,</div></div></body></html>
LOCATION:"Rennes-Salle Minquiers (B025\, Vidéoprojecteur )" <rennes-salle_mi
 nquiers@zimbra-local.inria.fr>
