BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cb638341-5f7e-47a8-94cb-940754771be5
SUMMARY:DiverSE Coffee
DESCRIPTION:Hi all\, \n\nWe'll have Pierre and Emmanuel in our DiverSE Coffe
 e tomorrow. Pierre will give a demo on Packer and Vagrant for virtual machin
 es and Emmanuel (new PhD student) will do a short presentation to introduce 
 himself.\n\nEnters @Pierre: In order to create an isolated environment with 
 specific dependencies\, one can use either virtualization or containerizatio
 n. Containers have fast boot times and a negligible overhead\, but they stil
 l depend on their host's hardware and need to interact directly with its ker
 nel. On the other hand\, virtual machines have worse performances\, but they
  offer more customization and reproducibility by simulating even the hardwar
 e. In the recent years\, Docker set a standard for containers by offering a 
 complete and unified ecosystem to automate their definition\, building\, sha
 ring and management. Here\, we will have a look at the association of Packer
  and Vagrant\, two complementary softwares that aim to create such an ecosys
 tem for virtual machines\, which can be used for packaging softwares\, artif
 acts or demonstrators among others.\n\nThe talk is held in room Aurigny at 1
  pm. \n\nKind regards\,\nJuliana.
LOCATION:"Rennes-Salle Aurigny (D165\, Vidéoprojecteur\, Visioconférence)" <
 rennes-salle_aurigny@zimbra-local.inria.fr>
ATTENDEE;CN=juliana alves-pereira;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=NEEDS-ACTION
 ;RSVP=TRUE:mailto:juliana.alves-pereira@irisa.fr
ATTENDEE;CN=diverse;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=NEEDS-ACTION;RSVP=TRUE:mai
 lto:diverse@inria.fr
ATTENDEE;CN="Rennes-Salle Aurigny (D165, Vidéoprojecteur, Visioconférence)";
 CUTYPE=RESOURCE;ROLE=NON-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=NEEDS-ACTION;RSVP=TRUE:mailto:
 rennes-salle_aurigny@zimbra-local.inria.fr
ORGANIZER;CN=Juliana Alves pereira:mailto:juliana.alves-pereira@irisa.fr
