BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:d0fd8a9d-e7f9-49d0-a998-6b378c7504f3
SUMMARY:DiverSE Coffee : Marcel Heinz
DESCRIPTION:Hi all\, \n\nWe are happy to receive Marcel Heinz as a guest spe
 aker for our next DiverSE Coffee. \n\nMarcel is a research assistant in the 
 software languages team at the University of Koblenz-Landau. He is working t
 owards a Ph.D. His general interests are in Software Language Engineering\, 
 Modeling and Ontologies. His research focus is on assisting at the comprehen
 sion of software technologies. \n\nEnters Marcel: \nWikipedia is a rich sour
 ce for classifying entities in many domains. Wikipedia's category graph focu
 ses on classification combined with secondary uses of categorization. \nWiki
 pedia's infoboxes define entity properties that also relate to classificatio
 n. In this paper\, we aim at validating and\, ultimately\, improving the cla
 ssification data available on Wikipedia. \nTo this end\, we develop a multi-
 dimensional methodology which combines available fragments of ground truth\,
  diverse feature extraction\, and metrics computation in a systematic manner
 . \nWe apply the methodology to a case study which results in a strongly val
 idated classification of software (computer) languages. \n\nThe Presentation
  is held this Friday in Markov room at 10 am. \n\nKind regards\, \n\n\n\n
