BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:d50a9abd-c7cd-485d-b8af-1339649531f9
SUMMARY:DiverSE Coffee : Kevin Corre
DESCRIPTION:Hi all\, \n\nOur fearless speaker\, Kevin Corre\, is closing the
  DiverSE Coffee for this academic year with an interesting talk on Why Users
  Cannot Choose their Identity Providers ( IdPs )on the Web\, and what can we
  do about it. \n\nTo answer this question\, Kevin conducted three investigat
 ions. The first one is a field survey on the scope usage of OAuth 2 and Open
 ID Connect by websites. This survey is intended to investigate if the scopes
  requested by websites allow for user-defined IdPs . \nThe second one tries 
 to understand whether the problem comes from the OAuth 2 protocol or its imp
 lementations by IdP\, while t he last one tries to understand if trust relat
 ions between websites and IdP could prevent the end user from selecting its 
 own IdP. \n\nKevin will be reporting on the results of his investigations\, 
 and propose an architecture for web browser-based identity management. \n\nT
 he presentation is Held in Room Markov\, Thursday\, July the 13th at 1 p.m. 
 \n\nDon't miss our last Coffee! \n\nCheers\, \n
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<html><body id='htmlmode'><h3>The following is 
 a new meeting request:</h3>\n\n<p>\n<table border='0'>\n<tr><th align=left>S
 ubject:</th><td>DiverSE Coffee : Kevin Corre </td></tr>\n<tr><th align=left>
 Organiser:</th><td>"Amine Benelallam" &lt\;amine.benelallam@inria.fr&gt\; </
 td></tr>\n</table>\n<p>\n<table border='0'>\n<tr><th align=left>Time:</th><t
 d>Thursday\, 13 July\, 2017\, 1:00:00 PM - 2:00:00 PM GMT +01:00 Brussels\, 
 Copenhagen\, Madrid\, Paris\n </td></tr></table>\n<p>\n<table border='0'>\n<
 tr><th align=left>Invitees:</th><td>diverse@inria.fr </td></tr>\n</table>\n<
 div>*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*</div><br><div style="font-family: times new roman\, 
 new york\, times\, serif\; font-size: 12pt\; color: #000000"><div>Hi all\,</
 div><div><br></div><div>Our fearless speaker\, Kevin Corre\, is closing the 
 DiverSE Coffee for this academic year with an interesting talk on&nbsp\;<str
 ong><span style="background-color: #ffffff\;" data-mce-style="background-col
 or: #ffffff\;">Why Users Cannot Choose their Identity Providers (IdPs)on the
  Web\, and what can we do about it.</span></strong><br></div><div><strong><s
 pan style="background-color: #ffffff\;" data-mce-style="background-color: #f
 fffff\;"><br></span></strong></div><div>To answer this question\, Kevin cond
 ucted three investigations. The first one is a field survey on the scope usa
 ge&nbsp\;of OAuth 2 and OpenID Connect by websites. This survey is intended 
 to investigate if the scopes requested by websites allow for user-defined&nb
 sp\;IdPs.</div><div>The second one tries to understand whether the problem c
 omes from the OAuth 2 protocol or its implementations by IdP\, while t<span 
 style="font-size: 12pt\;">he last one tries to understand if trust relations
  between websites and IdP could prevent the end user from selecting its own 
 IdP.&nbsp\;</span></div><div><span style="font-size: 12pt\;"><br></span></di
 v><div><span style="font-size: 12pt\;">Kevin will be reporting on the result
 s of his investigations\, and propose an architecture for web browser-based 
 identity management. &nbsp\;&nbsp\;</span></div><div><span style="font-size:
  12pt\;"><br></span></div><div><span style="font-size: 12pt\;">The presentat
 ion is Held in Room Markov\, &nbsp\;Thursday\, July the 13th at 1 p.m.</span
 ></div><div><br></div><div>Don't miss our last Coffee!</div><div><br></div><
 div>Cheers\,</div></div></body></html>
ATTENDEE;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=NEEDS-ACTION;RSVP=TRUE:mailto:diverse
 @inria.fr
ORGANIZER;CN=Amine Benelallam:mailto:amine.benelallam@inria.fr
