BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:d5489aa8-e6a9-42fd-b3a4-43a9a9bd5f7f
SUMMARY:[SEMINAR] Embedded DSLs generating (heterogeneous) efficient code (J
 . Richard Foy)
DESCRIPTION:Lightweight Modular Staging (LMS) is a Scala library that helps 
 to define high-level embedded DSLs without runtime overhead. From a practica
 l point of view\, LMS provides a way to define DSLs allowing to write differ
 ent aspects of a program\, to weave them and to generate efficient code (for
  potentially heterogeneous targets).\n
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<html><body><h3>La réunion suivante a été modif
 iée :</h3>\n\n<p>\n<table border='0'>\n<tr><th align=left>Sujet :</th><td>[S
 EMINAR] Embedded DSLs generating (heterogeneous) efficient code (J. Richard 
 Foy) [MODIFIÉ]</td></tr>\n<tr><th align=left>Organisateur:</th><td>"Benoit C
 ombemale" &lt\;benoit.combemale@irisa.fr&gt\; </td></tr>\n</table>\n<p>\n<ta
 ble border='0'>\n<tr><th align=left>Endroit :</th><td>"Rennes-Salle Lipari (
 F202)" &lt\;rennes-salle_lipari@zimbra-local.inria.fr&gt\; </td></tr>\n<tr><
 th align=left>Ressources :</th><td>"Rennes-Salle Lipari (F202)" &lt\;rennes-
 salle_lipari@zimbra-local.inria.fr&gt\; (Rennes-Salle Lipari (F202)) </td></
 tr>\n<tr><th align=left>Heure:</th><td>Mardi 28 Août 2012\, 13:00:00 - 14:00
 :00 GMT +01:00 Bruxelles\, Copenhague\, Madrid\, Paris\n </td></tr></table>\
 n<p>\n<table border='0'>\n<tr><th align=left>Invités:</th><td>thierry.boscha
 t@irisa.fr\; maxime.tricoire@inria.fr\; dionysios.efstathiou@irisa.fr\; seba
 stien.metay@irisa.fr\; pierre.despagne@inria.fr\; phillipa.bennett@inria.fr\
 ; fabio.buiati@irisa.fr\; marco.biazzini@inria.fr\; ivan.paez_anaya@irisa.fr
 \; erwan.bousse@gmail.com\; antonio-junior.mattos@irisa.fr ... </td></tr>\n<
 /table>\n<div>*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*</div><br>Lightweight Modular Staging (LMS)
  is a Scala library that helps to define high-level embedded DSLs without ru
 ntime overhead. From a practical point of view\, LMS provides a way to defin
 e DSLs allowing to write different aspects of a program\, to weave them and 
 to generate efficient code (for potentially heterogeneous targets).<br></bod
 y></html>
LOCATION:"Rennes-Salle Lipari (F202)" <rennes-salle_lipari@zimbra-local.inri
 a.fr>
