UID:d59c7292-8e5d-4fd0-aca0-0609b163b605
SUMMARY:Conf Lunch - Benoit Baudry
DESCRIPTION:How can ecologists and softwares engineers work together ? \n\nB
 enoit Baudry joined Inria in 2004. His research interests include software a
 nalysis and testing and model-driven engineering. He currently coordinates t
 he FP7 FET DIVERSIFY project\, which gathers an interdisciplinary consortium
  to investigate automated diversification for resilient software. He leads t
 he INRIA DiverSE team\, which includes 35 researchers and students investiga
 ting model-driven engineering and software product lines from requirements t
 o runtime. \n\n\nSoftware systems tend to favor large-scale monocultures. Fo
 r example\, web servers are highly dominated by one technology\, personnal c
 omputers by a single operating system or Wordpress sites by handful of plugi
 ns. While this is a great opportunity for maintenance and interoperability\,
  it is also a major risk for dependability\, e.g.\, the same bug is massivel
 y present in all distributions. During this Conf'lunch I will present this p
 henomenon and explain how the DIVERSIFY project investigates how the emergen
 ce of diversity in ecosystems can trigger new solutions to diversify softwar
 e. \n\n\n_______________________________________ \n\n\nDon't miss the new me
 eting Conf'Lunch on Friday\, October 10th 2014\, at 11 : 30 am in room Miche
 l Métivier. A cocktail lunch will be offered after the presentation. \n\nSo\
 , thank you to subscribe . \n\nIf you want to suggest a topic for conference
  and / or facilitate an event\, contact us. \n______________________________
 _________ \n\n\nThanks\, \n\nCoraline Lafon \nAssistante de communication \n
 \n
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<html><body id='htmlmode'><h3>Nouvelle demande 
 de réunion ci-dessous :</h3>\n\n<p>\n<table border='0'>\n<tr><th align=left>
 Sujet :</th><td>Conf Lunch - Benoit Baudry </td></tr>\n<tr><th align=left>Or
 ganisateur:</th><td>"Loic Lesage" &lt\;loic.lesage@inria.fr&gt\; </td></tr>\
 n</table>\n<p>\n<table border='0'>\n<tr><th align=left>Endroit :</th><td>Mét
 ivier </td></tr>\n<tr><th align=left>Heure:</th><td>Vendredi 10 Octobre 2014
 \, 11:30:00 - 13:00:00 GMT +01:00 Bruxelles\, Copenhague\, Madrid\, Paris\n 
 </td></tr></table>\n<p>\n<table border='0'>\n<tr><th align=left>Invités:</th
 ><td>ren-epi-diverse@zimbra-local.inria.fr </td></tr>\n</table>\n<div>*~*~*~
 *~*~*~*~*~*~*</div><br><div style="font-family: times new roman\, new york\,
  times\, serif\; font-size: 12pt\; color: #000000"><div><h4>How can ecologis
 ts and softwares engineers work together ?</h4><p style="margin: 0px\;" data
 -mce-style="margin: 0px\;"><strong>Benoit Baudry</strong> joined Inria in 20
 04. His research interests include software analysis and testing and model-d
 riven engineering. He currently coordinates the FP7 FET DIVERSIFY project\, 
 which gathers an interdisciplinary consortium to investigate automated diver
 sification for resilient software. He leads the INRIA DiverSE team\, which i
 ncludes 35 researchers and students investigating model-driven engineering a
 nd software product lines from requirements to runtime.</p><p style="margin:
  0px\;" data-mce-style="margin: 0px\;"><br></p><p style="margin: 0px\;" data
 -mce-style="margin: 0px\;"><strong>Software systems</strong> tend to favor l
 arge-scale monocultures. For example\, web servers are highly dominated by o
 ne technology\, personnal computers by a single operating system or Wordpres
 s sites by handful of plugins. While this is a great opportunity for mainten
 ance and interoperability\, it is also a major risk for dependability\, e.g.
 \, the same bug is massively present in all distributions. During this Conf'
 lunch I will present this phenomenon and explain how the DIVERSIFY project i
 nvestigates how the emergence of diversity in ecosystems can trigger new sol
 utions to diversify software.</p><p style="margin: 0px\;" data-mce-style="ma
 rgin: 0px\;"><br></p><p style="margin: 0px\;" data-mce-style="margin: 0px\;"
 >_______________________________________</p><p style="margin: 0px\;" data-mc
 e-style="margin: 0px\;"><br></p><p style="margin: 0px\;" data-mce-style="mar
 gin: 0px\;"><strong><em>Don't miss the new meeting Conf'Lunch on Friday\, Oc
 tober 10th 2014\, at 11 : 30 am in room Michel Métivier.</em></strong></p><h
 4><strong><em>A cocktail lunch will be offered after the presentation.</em> 
 </strong></h4><p style="margin: 0px\;" data-mce-style="margin: 0px\;"><stron
 g><em>So\, thank you to </em> <a href="mailto:coraline.lafon@inria.fr" rel="
 external" data-mce-href="mailto:coraline.lafon@inria.fr"><em>subscribe</em> 
 </a><em>.</em> </strong></p><p style="margin: 0px\;" data-mce-style="margin:
  0px\;"><strong><em>&nbsp\;</em></strong></p><p style="margin: 0px\;" data-m
 ce-style="margin: 0px\;"><strong><em>If you want to suggest a topic for conf
 erence and / or facilitate an event\, contact us.</em> </strong></p><p style
 ="margin: 0px\;" data-mce-style="margin: 0px\;"><strong><em>________________
 _______________________</em></strong></p><p style="margin: 0px\;" data-mce-s
 tyle="margin: 0px\;"><strong><em>&nbsp\;</em></strong></p><p style="margin: 
 0px\;" data-mce-style="margin: 0px\;"><strong><em>&nbsp\;</em></strong></p><
 p style="margin: 0px\;" data-mce-style="margin: 0px\;">Thanks\,<strong> <em>
 <br></em></strong></p><p style="margin: 0px\;" data-mce-style="margin: 0px\;
 "><strong><span style="font-family: trebuchet ms\,sans-serif\; font-size: sm
 all\;" face="trebuchet ms\,sans-serif" size="2" data-mce-style="font-family:
  trebuchet ms\,sans-serif\; font-size: small\;"><span style="font-family: tr
 ebuchet ms\,sans-serif\; font-size: small\;" face="trebuchet ms\,sans-serif"
  size="2" data-mce-style="font-family: trebuchet ms\,sans-serif\; font-size:
  small\;"><span class="Style4"><strong><strong>Coraline Lafon<br></strong></
 strong>Assistante de communication</span></span></span></strong></p><p style
 ="margin: 0px\;" data-mce-style="margin: 0px\;"><strong><em>&nbsp\;</em></st
 rong></p><p style="margin: 0px\;" data-mce-style="margin: 0px\;"><strong><em
 >&nbsp\;</em></strong></p></div></div></body></html>
