BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:e434211c-3f31-435a-8a58-2ae5f18f16f7
SUMMARY:DiverSe Coffee
DESCRIPTION:Hi everyone\, \n\nThis week the DiverSE Coffee will be presented
  by Stéphanie. \nDuring this coffee Stéphanie will talk about the formalizat
 ion of the Google Cloud Platform API specification. \nThis time the coffee w
 ill be in room Aurigny and broadcasted (A link will be shared the d-day) \n\
 nAbstract : \nGoogle Cloud Platform (GCP) is one of the leaders among cloud 
 APIs. It has gained notable expansion due to its suite of public cloud servi
 ces that it based on a huge\, solid infrastructure. GCP allows developers to
  use these services by accessing GCP RESTful API that is described through H
 TML pages on its website. However\, the documentation of GCP API is written 
 in natural language (English prose) and therefore shows several drawbacks\, 
 such as Informal Heterogeneous Documentation\, Imprecise Types\, Implicit At
 tribute Metadata\, Hidden Links\, Redundancy and Lack of Visual Support. To 
 avoid confusion and misunderstandings\, the cloud developers obviously need 
 a precise specification of the knowledge and activities in GCP. Therefore\, 
 this paper introduces GCP MODEL\, an inferred formal model-driven specificat
 ion of GCP which describes without ambiguity the resources offered by GCP. \
 n\nCheers\, \n\nGwendal \n
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<html><body id='htmlmode'><h3>La réunion suivan
 te a été transférée :</h3>\n\n<p>\n<table border='0'>\n<tr><th align=left>Su
 jet :</th><td>DiverSE Coffee </td></tr>\n<tr><th align=left>Organisateur:</t
 h><td>sophie.maupile@irisa.fr </td></tr>\n</table>\n<p>\n<table border='0'>\
 n<tr><th align=left>Endroit :</th><td>"Rennes-Salle Aurigny (D165\, Vidéopro
 jecteur\, Visioconférence)" &lt\;rennes-salle_aurigny@zimbra-local.inria.fr&
 gt\; </td></tr>\n<tr><th align=left>Ressources :</th><td>"Rennes-Salle Aurig
 ny (D165\, Vidéoprojecteur\, Visioconférence)" &lt\;rennes-salle_aurigny@zim
 bra-local.inria.fr&gt\; (Rennes-Salle Aurigny (D165\, Vidéoprojecteur\, Visi
 oconférence)) </td></tr>\n<tr><th align=left>Heure:</th><td>Jeudi 24 Septemb
 re 2020\, 13:00:00 - 14:00:00 GMT +01:00 Bruxelles\, Copenhague\, Madrid\, P
 aris\n </td></tr></table>\n<p>\n<table border='0'>\n<tr><th align=left>Invit
 és:</th><td>gwendal.jouneaux@irisa.fr\; diverse@inria.fr </td></tr>\n</table
 >\n<div>*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*</div><br><div style="font-family: arial\, helvet
 ica\, sans-serif\; font-size: 12pt\; color: #000000"><div>Hi everyone\,</div
 ><div><br data-mce-bogus="1"></div><div>This week the DiverSE Coffee will be
  presented by Stéphanie.<br></div><div>During this coffee Stéphanie will tal
 k about the formalization of the Google Cloud Platform API specification.</d
 iv><div>This time the coffee will be in room Aurigny and broadcasted (A link
  will be shared the d-day)<br data-mce-bogus="1"></div><div><br data-mce-bog
 us="1"></div><div>Abstract :<br>Google Cloud Platform (GCP) is one of the le
 aders among cloud APIs. It \nhas gained notable expansion due to its suite o
 f public cloud services \nthat it based on a huge\, solid infrastructure. GC
 P allows developers to \nuse these services by accessing GCP RESTful API tha
 t is described \nthrough HTML pages on its website. However\, the documentat
 ion of GCP API\n is written in natural language (English prose) and therefor
 e shows \nseveral drawbacks\, such as Informal Heterogeneous Documentation\,
  \nImprecise Types\, Implicit Attribute Metadata\, Hidden Links\, Redundancy
  \nand Lack of Visual Support. To avoid confusion and misunderstandings\, \n
 the cloud developers obviously need a precise specification of the \nknowled
 ge and activities in GCP. Therefore\, this paper introduces GCP \nMODEL\, an
  inferred formal model-driven specification of GCP which \ndescribes without
  ambiguity the resources offered by GCP.</div><div><br data-mce-bogus="1"></
 div><div>Cheers\,<br data-mce-bogus="1"></div><div><br data-mce-bogus="1"></
 div><div>Gwendal<br data-mce-bogus="1"></div></div></body></html>
LOCATION:"Rennes-Salle Aurigny (D165\, Vidéoprojecteur\, Visioconférence)" <
 rennes-salle_aurigny@zimbra-local.inria.fr>
