BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:e6e3a40b-f6f4-4b5c-a7a8-09b36326e225
SUMMARY:Compiling Product Lines: The Case of Web Configurators
DESCRIPTION:Ongoing progress meeting \n\nThis can be seen as an internal dea
 dline. \nIdeally speaking I hope we can implement our first re-engineering o
 f one configurator \n* Mai should provide the CVL specification (using MDE t
 echnology)\, related artefacts (visual elements\, javascript functions\, etc
 .) and some explanations on how we could compile a web solution from a CVL m
 odel \n* Bosco and me are focusing on Scala implementation of VAM\, VRM and 
 "artefacts" \n* Julien should exploit a CVL specification (specified in Scal
 a) and develop a specific compiler capable of reproducing the targeted confi
 gurator \n\nWe have to collaborate all together of course \;-) \nNote also t
 hat I (and others?) will try to put our ideas in a more formal form. \n\nMat
 hieu \n\n\n
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<html><body><h3>La réunion suivante a été modif
 iée :</h3>\n\n<p>\n<table border='0'>\n<tr><th align=left>Sujet :</th><td>Co
 mpiling Product Lines: The Case of Web Configurators </td></tr>\n<tr><th ali
 gn=left>Organisateur:</th><td>"Mathieu Acher" &lt\;mathieu.acher@irisa.fr&gt
 \; </td></tr>\n</table>\n<p>\n<table border='0'>\n<tr><th align=left>Endroit
  :</th><td>"Rennes-Salle Lipari (F202)" &lt\;rennes-salle_lipari@zimbra-loca
 l.inria.fr&gt\; [MODIFIÉ]</td></tr>\n<tr><th align=left>Ressources :</th><td
 >"Rennes-Salle Lipari (F202)" &lt\;rennes-salle_lipari@zimbra-local.inria.fr
 &gt\; (Lieu : Rennes\, Bâtiment : F\, Étage : orange\, Salle : F202) [MODIFI
 É]</td></tr>\n<tr><th align=left>Heure:</th><td>Lundi 15 Juillet 2013\, 15:0
 0:00 - 16:00:00 GMT +01:00 Bruxelles\, Copenhague\, Madrid\, Paris [MODIFIÉ]
 \n </td></tr></table>\n<p>\n<table border='0'>\n<tr><th align=left>Invités:<
 /th><td>marianela.ciolfi-felice@inria.fr\; julien.richard-foy@irisa.fr\; joa
 o.ferreira_filho@inria.fr\; benoit.combemale@irisa.fr\; olivier.barais@irisa
 .fr </td></tr>\n</table>\n<div>*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*</div><br>Ongoing progress
  meeting <br><br>This can be seen as an internal deadline. <br>Ideally speak
 ing I hope we can implement our first re-engineering of one configurator <br
 >* Mai should provide the CVL specification (using MDE technology)\, related
  artefacts (visual elements\, javascript functions\, etc.) and some explanat
 ions on how we could compile a web solution from a CVL model <br>* Bosco and
  me are focusing on Scala implementation of VAM\, VRM and "artefacts" <br>* 
 Julien should exploit a CVL specification (specified in Scala) and develop a
  specific compiler capable of reproducing the targeted configurator <br><br>
 We have to collaborate all together of course \;-) <br>Note also that I (and
  others?) will try to put our ideas in a more formal form. <br><br>Mathieu <
 br><br><br></body></html>
