BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ea7dcef2-d28a-4d08-aee8-c20a5cc29845
SUMMARY:DiverSE Coffee [Oscar]: Pit internals\, how to add new mutation oper
 ators
DESCRIPTION:Hi all\, \n\nTo answer the many questions that have been raised 
 during the previous DiverSE Coffee about PITest internals\, we decided to fo
 llow-up with a dedicated session. \nMany thanks to Oscar for accepting to cl
 arify these points. \n\n\nEnters Oscar: \n"PITest is a state-of-the-art muta
 tion testing tool for Java projects. It provides off-the-shelf functionaliti
 es. It also offers mechanisms to add new features through a plugin system. \
 nThere are two main approaches to add new mutation operators. One of them is
  to modify the existing code base and the other one is to create a plugin th
 at handles the discovery of potential mutants and ultimately apply the corre
 sponding transformations. In this session\, we will explore the pros and con
 s of both solutions." \n\nThe presentation is held this Thursday in room Min
 quiers at 1 p.m. \n\nKind regards\, \n
LOCATION:"Rennes-Salle Minquiers (B025)" <rennes-salle_minquiers@zimbra-loca
 l.inria.fr>
ATTENDEE;CN=Oscar;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=ACCEPTED:mailto:oscar.vera-p
 erez@inria.fr
ATTENDEE;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=NEEDS-ACTION;RSVP=TRUE:mailto:diverse
 @inria.fr
ATTENDEE;CN=Alejandro Gomez boix;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=ACCEPTED:mail
 to:alejandro.gomez-boix@inria.fr
ATTENDEE;CN=Rennes-Salle Minquiers (B025);CUTYPE=RESOURCE;ROLE=NON-PARTICIPA
 NT;PARTSTAT=ACCEPTED;RSVP=TRUE:mailto:rennes-salle_minquiers@zimbra-local.in
 ria.fr
ORGANIZER;CN=Amine Benelallam:mailto:amine.benelallam@inria.fr
