BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:eb552634-a3ab-4eaa-8e28-ef37e376d41f
SUMMARY:DiverSE Coffee[JED]: Using Quantile Regression for Reclaiming Unused
  Cloud Resources while achieving SLA
DESCRIPTION:Hi all\, \n\nIn two weeks time\, Jean Emile Dartois will be pres
 enting his latest accepted paper in CLOUDCOM entitled: Using Quantile Regres
 sion for Reclaiming Unused Cloud Resources while achieving SLA. \n\nEnters E
 mile: " Although Cloud computing techniques have reduced the total cost of o
 wnership thanks to virtualization\, the average usage of resources (e.g.\, C
 PU\, RAM\, Network\, I/O) remains low. To address such issue\, one may sell 
 unused resources. Such a solution requires the Cloud provider to determine t
 he resources available and estimate their future use to provide availability
  guarantees. This paper proposes a technique that uses machine learning algo
 rithms (Random Forest\, Gradient Boosting Decision Tree\, and Long Short Ter
 m Memory) to forecast 24-hour of available resources at the host level. Our 
 technique relies on the use of quantile regression to provide a flexible tra
 de-off between the potential amount of resources to reclaim and the risk of 
 SLA violations. In addition\, several metrics (e.g.\, CPU\, RAM\, disk\, net
 work) were predicted to provide exhaustive availability guarantees. Our meth
 odology was evaluated by relying on four in production data center traces an
 d our results show that quantile regression is relevant to reclaim unused re
 sources. Our approach may increase the amount of savings up to 20% compared 
 to traditional approaches. " \n\nThe presentation is held Thursday\, Decembe
 r 6\, in room Lipari at 1 pm. \n\nRegards\, \n
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<html><body id='htmlmode'><h3>The following mee
 ting has been modified:</h3>\n\n<p>\n<table border='0'>\n<tr><th align=left>
 Subject:</th><td>DiverSE Coffee[JED]: Using Quantile Regression for Reclaimi
 ng Unused Cloud Resources while achieving SLA </td></tr>\n<tr><th align=left
 >Organiser:</th><td>"Amine Benelallam" &lt\;amine.benelallam@inria.fr&gt\; <
 /td></tr>\n</table>\n<p>\n<table border='0'>\n<tr><th align=left>Location:</
 th><td>"Rennes-Salle Lipari (F202 Vidéoprojecteur\, Visioconférence)" &lt\;r
 ennes-salle_lipari@zimbra-local.inria.fr&gt\; [MODIFIED]</td></tr>\n<tr><th 
 align=left>Resources:</th><td>"Rennes-Salle Lipari (F202 Vidéoprojecteur\, V
 isioconférence)" &lt\;rennes-salle_lipari@zimbra-local.inria.fr&gt\; (Lieu :
  Rennes\, Bâtiment : F\, Étage : orange\, Salle : F202) [MODIFIED]</td></tr>
 \n<tr><th align=left>Time:</th><td>Thursday\, 6 December\, 2018\, 13:00:00 -
  14:00:00 GMT +01:00 Brussels\, Copenhagen\, Madrid\, Paris [MODIFIED]\n </t
 d></tr></table>\n<p>\n<table border='0'>\n<tr><th align=left>Invitees:</th><
 td>diverse@inria.fr </td></tr>\n</table>\n<div>*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*</div><br>
 <div style="font-family: arial\, helvetica\, sans-serif\; font-size: 12pt\; 
 color: #000000"><div style="font-family: arial\, helvetica\, sans-serif\; fo
 nt-size: 12pt\; color: #000000\;" data-mce-style="font-family: arial\, helve
 tica\, sans-serif\; font-size: 12pt\; color: #000000\;"><div>Hi all\,&nbsp\;
 </div><div><br></div><div>In two weeks time\, Jean Emile Dartois will be pre
 senting his latest accepted paper in CLOUDCOM entitled:&nbsp\;Using Quantile
  Regression for Reclaiming Unused Cloud Resources while achieving SLA.<br><b
 r>Enters Emile: " Although Cloud computing techniques have reduced the total
  cost of ownership thanks to virtualization\, the average usage of resources
  (e.g.\, CPU\, RAM\, Network\, I/O) remains low. To address such issue\, one
  may sell unused resources. Such a solution requires the Cloud provider to d
 etermine the resources available and estimate their future use to provide av
 ailability guarantees. This paper proposes a technique that uses machine lea
 rning algorithms (Random Forest\, Gradient Boosting Decision Tree\, and Long
  Short Term Memory) to forecast 24-hour of available resources at the host l
 evel. Our technique relies on the use of quantile regression to provide a fl
 exible trade-off between the potential amount of resources to reclaim and th
 e risk of SLA violations. In addition\, several metrics (e.g.\, CPU\, RAM\, 
 disk\, network) were predicted to provide exhaustive availability guarantees
 . Our methodology was evaluated by relying on four in production data center
  traces and our results show that quantile regression is relevant to reclaim
  unused resources. Our approach may increase the amount of savings up to 20%
  compared to traditional approaches. "</div><div><br></div><div>The presenta
 tion is&nbsp\;held Thursday\, December 6\, in room&nbsp\;Lipari at 1 pm.<br>
 <br>Regards\,</div></div></div></body></html>
LOCATION:"Rennes-Salle Lipari (F202 Vidéoprojecteur\, Visioconférence)" <ren
 nes-salle_lipari@zimbra-local.inria.fr>
