BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:f2279c72-81e1-4c86-b080-34a9c4eb4034
SUMMARY:Diverse Coffee
DESCRIPTION:Hi all\, \n\nYoussou Ndiaye is our next DiverSE Coffee speaker. 
 He will present his SAC'19 paper "Requirements for preventing logic flaws in
  the authentication procedure of Web Applications".\n\nEnters @Youssou: "Ens
 uring the security is one of the most daunting challenges that web applicati
 ons are facing nowadays. Authentication and authorization are two main secur
 ity fields that web applications must consider to be protected against unaut
 horized accesses. Various approaches that detect well-known vulnerabilities 
 and flaws exist. However\, these approaches mainly focus on detecting input 
 validation flaws. Another kind of flaws that affect web applications are log
 ic flaws\, but they lack of considerations. This paper proposes an approach 
 that helps to considering logic flaws in the context of web applications. Th
 e goal of the proposal is to strengthen the authentication procedure of web 
 applications and thus enforce the security early in the design phase. We con
 ducted an empirical study in nine well-known web-based applications to demon
 strate that logic flaws may put at risk the authentication procedure. The re
 sults showed that logic flaws may be either caused by security issues or usa
 bility issues. To overcome such flaws\, we provide relevant requirements tha
 t should be followed in the design of an authentication procedure."\n\nThe p
 resentation is held this Thursday\, April 4th in room Sardaigne at 1 pm.\n\n
 Kind regards\,\nJuliana.\n\n
LOCATION:"Rennes-Salle Sardaigne (F102\, Vidéoprojecteur\, Visioconférence)"
  <rennes-salle_sardaigne@zimbra-local.inria.fr>
ATTENDEE;CN=diverse;PARTSTAT=NEEDS-ACTION;RSVP=TRUE:mailto:diverse@inria.fr
ATTENDEE;CN=Youssou Ndiaye;PARTSTAT=NEEDS-ACTION;RSVP=TRUE:mailto:youssou.nd
 iaye@irisa.fr
X-MS-OLK-SENDER:mailto:juliana.alves-pereira@irisa.fr
ORGANIZER;CN=Fanny Banor;SENT-BY="mailto:juliana.alves-pereira@irisa.fr":mai
 lto:fanny.banor@irisa.fr
X-MS-OLK-SENDER:mailto:juliana.alves-pereira@irisa.fr
DTSTART;TZID="Europe/Brussels":20190404T130000
DTEND;TZID="Europe/Brussels":20190404T143000
