DESCRIPTION:update\, the program: \n\nDec. 6th : \n\n14:00-14:30: Short intr
 oduction\, and overview of the research activities in the Inria/IRISA DiverS
 E research group (Benoit Combemale\, Inria) \n14:30-15:00: Overview of the r
 esearch activity related to environment modeling and tradeoff analysis\, and
  overview of the related challenges (Jean-Raynald de Dreuzy\, OSUR) \n14:30-
 15:00: Overview of the research activity related to tradeoff analysis\, and 
 overview of the related challenges (Francois Pinet\, IRSTEA) \n15:30-16:00: 
 coffee break \n16:00-17:00: Participative modeling\, model coordination and 
 tradeoff analysis. The role of Serious Game (Laure Vidaud\, IRSTEA) \n17:00-
 18:00: Discussions (all) \n\nDec. 7th : \n\n09:00-09:45: Discussion: Global 
 Modeling\, Domain-Specific Modeling Languages\, Serious Game\, Open Data (al
 l) \n09:45-10:30: Discussion: Scientific modeling and related software techn
 ology challenges\, incl. cloud\, HPC\, etc. (all) \n10:30-11:00: coffee brea
 k \n11:00-12:30: — TBC — \n12:30-14:00: lunch \n14:00-15:30: Wrap-up: big pi
 cture\, research statement\, manifesto\, roadmap… and future actions (all) \
 n15:30-16:00: coffee break and final discussions \n\n\n--- \n\nHi all\, \n\n
 Laure Vidaud and her supervisor Francois Pinet\, both from IRSTEA and part o
 f IDM4SCO (http://gemoc.org/idm4sco/)\, are visiting us on Dec. 6th (startin
 g at 2pm ) and 7th (finishing at 4pm ). \nThe program will come ASAP\, but t
 he main objective is to share about our respective experiences on the use of
  models for environmental sciences and tradeoff analysis. \n\nLaure is also 
 very interested in learning on MDE technologies (Didier\, would you have som
 e time to help her???!!!). \n\nPlease\, let me know if you will attend the m
 eeting such as I can organize the lunch. \n\nThanks\, \nbenoit \n
