BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:f650cf74-21aa-40b7-bf43-a6562b874bbd
SUMMARY:[SEMINAR] Work on Software Product Line Testing at SINTEF (Martin Fa
 gereng Johansen)
DESCRIPTION:\nMartin Johansen has been working on the problem of testing sof
 tware product lines for two years for his PhD and as a part of the European 
 VERDE project. The work has had a strong focus on empirics for driving the r
 esearch. The first part of the work used empirics in two ways\, (1) to see w
 hat industry does today with regards to testing their product lines and ther
 eby what is lacking\, and (2) an evaluation of academic suggestions for how 
 to do product lines testing. This work resulted in the decision to move forw
 ard with combinatorial interaction testing. The second part of the work used
  empirics to investigate combinatorial interaction testing by generating cov
 ering arrays from realistic feature models. The feature models were gathered
  from industry and research. This work resulted in an analysis of the proper
 ties of realistic feature and the conclusion that combinatorial interaction 
 testing is tractable for realistic product lines. Current work is focused on
  improving the generation of covering arrays based on our analysis so far. \
 n
LOCATION:Rennes-Salle Lipari (F202)
