BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:fef0c3df-3102-408c-87b3-87b3e55d910e
SUMMARY:DiverSe Coffee
DESCRIPTION:Hi all\,\n\nFor the DiverSE coffee of this week\, Pierre will in
 troduce his vision on domain-specific language protocols.\nLike last time\, 
 this coffee will be limited to 14 people in the room.\nOf course\, we will b
 roadcast this presentation (better than last time\, I swear)\n\nAbstract :\n
 Protocols were defined by IDE manufacturers to reuse environment-agnostic la
 nguage\ncomponents: the most notable is the Language Server Protocol (LSP) f
 or textual editors\nand the Debug Adapter Protocol (DAP) for debugging facil
 ities.\nThese are well suited for most general purpose languages that share 
 a common set of\nfixed capabilities (e.g.\, textual syntax\, explicit contro
 l flow)\, but they are limited\nin the support of the very heterogeneous ser
 vices commonly found in domain-specific\nlanguages (DSL).\nIn order to manag
 e the interactions between a generic development environment and the\nlangua
 ge components available for a DSL\, we explore the ability to establish\ndom
 ain-specific language protocols.\nWe consider an approach in which a languag
 e server is defined by a microservices\narchitecture\, taking into account c
 oncerns about distribution\, extensibility and\nscalability\, and in which t
 he protocol emerges from the orchestration.\n\nCheers\,\n\n\nGwendal JOUNEAU
 X\n\n
LOCATION:"Rennes-Salle Markov (G105\, Vidéoprojecteur) [R]" <rennes-salle_ma
 rkov@zimbra-local.inria.fr>
ATTENDEE;CN=diverse;PARTSTAT=NEEDS-ACTION;RSVP=TRUE:mailto:diverse@inria.fr
X-MS-OLK-SENDER:mailto:gwendal.jouneaux@irisa.fr
ORGANIZER;CN=Sophie Maupile;SENT-BY="mailto:gwendal.jouneaux@irisa.fr":mailt
 o:sophie.maupile@irisa.fr
X-MS-OLK-SENDER:mailto:gwendal.jouneaux@irisa.fr
