BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ff5d6374-7dc8-434b-94fc-dda5b73f9d39
SUMMARY:DiverSE Coffee: Pierre  Laperdrix
DESCRIPTION:Hi all\, \n\nOur speaker for this week's coffee\, Pierre Laperdr
 ix\, will be presenting his latest work on browser fingerprinting: \n"FPRand
 om: Randomizing core browser objects to break advanced device fingerprinting
  techniques" \n\nHis work aims at mitigating the risk of browser fingerprint
 ing by introducing randomness in the computation of selected browser functio
 ns\, and thus\, breaking the stability of a fingerprint over time. \n\nKudos
  to Pierre! \n\nEnters Pierre: \n\n\n"The rich programming interfaces (APIs)
  provided by web browsers can be diverted to collect a browser fingerprint. 
 A small number of queries on these interfaces are sufficient to build a fing
 erprint that is statistically unique and very stable over time. Consequently
 \, the fingerprint can be used to track users. I'll now continue with nonsen
 se to see if people reAd the coffee's summaRy. And of course\, sorry to meta
 models and DSLs lovers\, my coffee is about browser fiNgerprinting and stuff
 . I don't know whAt you expected. I coUld now try to make some stupiD jokes 
 but no\, I prefer to take thIS opportunity to thank AMine \nfor his help org
 anizing the coffee everY week. And don't botHer looking for a secrEt message
  in this mail\, I conveRted random letters to uppercase letters just to mess
  with yOu. See you on Thursday!" \n\n\n\n\nThe presentation is likely held i
 n Markov Room\, Thursday\, June 29th at 1 p.m. \n\n\nSee you there\, \n
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<html><body id='htmlmode'><h3>The following is 
 a new meeting request:</h3>\n\n<p>\n<table border='0'>\n<tr><th align=left>S
 ubject:</th><td>DiverSE Coffee: Pierre  Laperdrix </td></tr>\n<tr><th align=
 left>Organiser:</th><td>"Amine Benelallam" &lt\;amine.benelallam@inria.fr&gt
 \; </td></tr>\n</table>\n<p>\n<table border='0'>\n<tr><th align=left>Time:</
 th><td>Thursday\, 29 June\, 2017\, 1:00:00 PM - 2:00:00 PM GMT +01:00 Brusse
 ls\, Copenhagen\, Madrid\, Paris\n </td></tr></table>\n<p>\n<table border='0
 '>\n<tr><th align=left>Invitees:</th><td>pierre.laperdrix@inria.fr\; diverse
 @inria.fr </td></tr>\n</table>\n<div>*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*</div><br><div style
 ="font-family: times new roman\, new york\, times\, serif\; font-size: 12pt\
 ; color: #000000"><div style="font-family: times new roman\, new york\, time
 s\, serif\; font-size: 12pt\; color: #000000"><div>Hi all\,&nbsp\;</div><div
 ><br></div><div>Our speaker for this week's coffee\, Pierre Laperdrix\, will
  be presenting his latest work on browser fingerprinting:</div><div><span st
 yle="font-size: 12pt\;">"FPRandom: Randomizing core browser objects to break
  advanced device fingerprinting techniques"</span></div><div><span style="fo
 nt-size: 12pt\;"><br></span></div><div><span style="font-size: 12pt\;">His w
 ork aims at mitigating the risk of browser fingerprinting by introducing ran
 domness in the computation of selected browser functions\, and thus\, breaki
 ng the stability of a fingerprint over time.&nbsp\;&nbsp\;</span></div><div>
 <br></div><div>Kudos to Pierre!&nbsp\;</div><div><br></div><div>Enters Pierr
 e:&nbsp\;</div><div><br></div><div><p style="margin: 0px\;" data-mce-style="
 margin: 0px\;">"The rich programming interfaces (APIs) provided by web brows
 ers can be diverted to collect a browser fingerprint. A small number of quer
 ies on these interfaces are sufficient to build a fingerprint that is statis
 tically unique and very stable over time. Consequently\, the fingerprint can
  be used to track users. I'll now continue with nonsense to see if people re
 Ad the coffee's summaRy. And of course\, sorry to metamodels and DSLs lovers
 \, my coffee is about browser fiNgerprinting and stuff. I don't know whAt yo
 u expected. I coUld now try to make some stupiD jokes but no\, I prefer to t
 ake thIS opportunity to thank AMine<br>for his help organizing the coffee ev
 erY week. And don't botHer looking for a secrEt message in this mail\, I con
 veRted random letters to uppercase letters just to mess with yOu. See you on
  Thursday!"</p><p style="margin: 0px\;" data-mce-style="margin: 0px\;"><br><
 /p><p style="margin: 0px\;" data-mce-style="margin: 0px\;"><br></p><p style=
 "margin: 0px\;" data-mce-style="margin: 0px\;">The presentation is likely he
 ld in Markov Room\, Thursday\, June 29th at 1 p.m.</p><p style="margin: 0px\
 ;" data-mce-style="margin: 0px\;"><br></p><p style="margin: 0px\;" data-mce-
 style="margin: 0px\;"><span style="font-size: 12pt\;">See you there\,</span>
 </p></div></div></div></body></html>
